{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions","id":799156,"title":"[2e] Werewolf Crossover Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-03T01:18:48-08:00","id":799156,"title":"[2e] Werewolf Crossover Questions","content":"Picture the scene. Kindred hold one section of an American city while a Werewolf pack has started moving in, claiming feeding grounds as their own territory and almost daring the Kindred to stop them. The Coterie that claims that feeding ground starts by trying to prevent the situation escalating too far - knowing full well Werewolves are both temperamental and extremely dangerous. The Coterie is BP1, 2 or 3, 2 Crone, 1 Ordo and 1 Carthian, 1 Ventrue, 1 Gangrel (Ordo, frenzy monster style), Daeva and a Mekhet.<br /> <br /> Can you suggest - with brief examples, far too often people say 'use your political powers to win' without specifics - ways to stall out and reverse the expansion of the Werewolves without escalating too much and avoiding combat where possible.<br /> <br /> Then, later, a Death Raging Werewolf has killed two of the Coterie's Touchstones, escalating the situation to boiling point. Now the Kindred want the Werewolves dead. Chasing them off won't be enough - an injured enemy comes back for revenge. Knowing the Werewolves can hunt them down with their fantastic senses the Kindred need a way of staying safe while launching attacks that will end with dead Werewolves...without dying themselves.<br /> <br /> Can you suggest some approaches - with examples - how the Kindred can stay safe from these wolves while also killing them.<br /> <br /> These Werewolves would eventually go scorched earth, destroy the Kindred at any cost etc. so violence spiral should be included in the planning.<br /> <br /> While I've got your attention a question about mechanics.<br /> 1. Werewolf claws from their non-Hishu forms deal Lethal, or is it treated as Bashing to Kindred?<br /> 2. Can Blood Sorcery (as seen in the splat book, not just the ones in the core) affect Spirits and/or Ghosts? Any suggestions as to how?<br /> 3. When a werewolf transforms do they shift their carried stuff with them? If yes would a smartphone or other broadcasting device still be broadcasting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T02:44:24-08:00","id":799239,"title":"","content":"Assuming that the Werewolves have Wolf-Blooded pack members and allies, have vampires target their enemy through them. The right mix of Dominate, Majesty, Vinculum, and Vitae Addiction should give the Kindred an edge. And that's not counting in the ghouls who can act in their stead during the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T02:46:43-08:00","id":799240,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it's just their teeth that do lethal. Some sort of symbolic predator thing. Blood sorcery can probably affect the right sort of spirit, and as for carried stuff, it would definitely stay on them in Dalu. I think they can choose not to shift with stuff in the case of the other three forms (at the very least holding the item in their mouth should work) and there's always fetishes to muck around with otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T03:39:00-08:00","id":799344,"title":"","content":"Focusing on just the mechanics<br /> <br /> <b>Tooth and Claw - </b>In Werewolf 2e, it is explicitly called out that the teeth of a werewolf in every form (including Hishu) deal supernatural damage. The claws soften a target up, bit Werewolves kill with their teeth. A Vampires resistance to mundane damage would protect them from a werewolves claws in most situations. I would make exceptions for when the Werewolf uses Gifts to augment their damage (such as Crushing Blow or Rending Claws), and for when the Werewolf has gone into <i>Basu-Im</i> (Death Rage).<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Sorcery</b> - Generally speaking, Vampire Magic focuses on channeling the Curse, and has limited capabilities to effect the Spirit world. A Vampire occultist would have to deal with ephemeral creatures using the methods and techniques available to mortal occultists [See Mortal Interaction in the Ephemeral Entities section of the appropriate books].<br /> While they have not been updated to 2e, the Circle of the Crone book has several rituals that explicitly interact with spirits ( pages.201-204) they are considered optional, since Spirit Magic is more of a Mage or Werewolf thing. <br /> <br /> <b>Shifting</b> - As of second edition, a Werewolf at most harmony levels ( 8 or less) shifts with them. Belongings in Dalu (Near Human) adjust to fit,but would be otherwise functional.Belongings in Gauru (Warform), Urshul (Near-Wolf) and Urhan (Wolf) are subsumed into the werewolves essence and become non-functional in all respects. So trying to track a werewolf by cellphone signal is a frustrating exercise where the signal vanishes seemingly at random.<br /> <br /> <b>General Advice for Vampires</b><ul><li>Avoid head to head fight - unless you can secure a distinct tactical advantage. An individual Vampire warrior can be more than a match for a Uratha, but this represent a specialized skill set. Even a Werewolf accountant can turn into a killer at the drop of a hat. If the Vampires do not have access to reliable silver weapons, cannot marshal a force of their deadliest warriors, or cannot draft minions that won't lose their minds with Lunacy, try to use diplomacy or social attacks.</li> <li>Know your Limits - I have run many a Vampire game where the group mystic wants to beat the Werewolves at their own game. This is almost always a mistake. Under the best of circumstances a Vampires spirit arsenal is limited vs a Werewolf who's entire arsenal IS spirit. Learn a trick or two, use it when needed, but for the most part don't invest heavily in this tactic.</li> <li>Use your strength - Vampires excel at influence, manipulation, and twisting mortal society around their fingers. Most Vampires have some investment in social merits (Allies, Contacts, Mentors, Retainers, Resources, Staff). Use these to counter and undermine The Werewolves resources. Use Disciplines, Bribery, Coercion and Extortion to undermine their non - Uratha and entirely mortal support base. Heck, use these resources against the Uratha themselves! Don't think of the Werewolves as invading Orcs, but as individuals. And every individual has a price. No other supernatural group is as invested in the structure of mortal society,and no other group can weapon that society as easily or as well.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T04:07:52-08:00","id":799465,"title":"","content":"I think the first issue here is that we're assuming a violent death spiral here. Vampires are the Social splat, whereas Wolves are the Physical. The vamps are best suited to win through non-physical means. Take a look at Dominate, Majesty, etc. Most start failing to work in combat. So stay out of it. Meet somewhere the wolves won't be eager to attack - or find someway to meet in relative safety. Once there, the vamps have the advantage socially. Vampire obfuscate is leagues better than Uratha stealth, and following one around is good, and most Insight Gifts are unsuited for calling for Clash of Wills here; yes, they could use Scent the Unnatural, but that costs Essence to activate, and the vampire is simply unnoticable, so little reason to activate it in the first place. Boundry Ward is probably the best detection method, but even that is questionable in this case.<br /> <br /> I disagree on the notion that most vamps have mortal influences, but it absolutely is a major selling point of the Invictus and Movement. That said, Elodoth and Iron Masters excell at using webs of social influence to hunt - I am going to assume that is a wash. Werewolves can recruit spirits, but vampire blood magics can call upon the Strix. And werewolves are just as susceptable to attacks by the Owls as the vampires are to spirits. Like social influences, I'm going to call this one a wash - something both groups are good at.<br /> <br /> This is completely ignoring a vampire's greatest weapon - the Vinculum and the Kiss. The Kindred excell at corruption and twiting others to their cause. A daeva with Kiss of the Succubus can supernaturally addict a wolf to being fed on; they won't want to kill. You can establish three drinks blood bond in the course of minutes, no three nights required. And, once bonded, you can use Social Maneuvering to get the bonded wolf to do anything practically. Get the wolves together, you can Dominate/Majesty them as a group, then Kiss and bond them. Or individually. If you absolutely must kill the wolves, then once you've got them under your control, separate and feed on them to death. They won't struggle at that point.<br /> <br /> Where vampire blood magic really shines in this scenario, in my opinion, is the number of divinations that are available. Werewolves are good at sensing things in their territory after a bit of set up, and general threats. Vampires, on the other hand, can figure out the best way to approach the wolves in the first place through signs and portents on a level the wolves can't. Forget the rituals in the core book - convert some from the Blood Sorcery book and look at the spoilers for Secrets of the Covenant. Even if a PC personally doesn't know an appropriate ritual, an elder would, and will likely cast it for a favor.* There's a number of abilities there that are just gorgeous at tracking down the wolves from a distance. Hells, track down just one member of their pack, even if its just a wolf blooded. Alone, you can corrupt that one member, and you've got the initiative on the rest with information and blackmail and misdirection.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Only teeth, acording to the sidebar. Which is notable, because Garou powers often increase claw attack power, but they're still only bashing to the Kindred.<br /> 2. Blood Sorcery could affect spirits or ghosts, but you'd have to make new rituals for it. Generally speaking, most groups stick to their own powers. Of note, however, is that spirits and ghosts are affected by vampire Discipliens as easily as mortals. You can Dominate a spirit, you can Majesty it, you can Obfuscate from them and you can Nightmare them.<br /> 3. I assume you're talking about the vanishing clothes when they shift into a more wolfy form. I would say that the electronics vanish, then reappear when they assume a Hishu or Dalu form.<br /> <br /> * I've often seen Werewolf fans in the past claim that werewolves are better social creatures than vampires, because the pack sticks together while vamps tend to backstab. What doesn't come up is that vampires have much better support structure with more powerful of their kind to call upon in times of need than a wolf will. Any vamp can look to his covenant mates. Its rare for wolves to call for help outside their territory. The covenant support structure is a huge boon to vampires as part of that whole Social splat thing I mentioned above, and one I suggest your vampire PCs take advantage of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-03-2016, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T04:40:11-08:00","id":799513,"title":"","content":"Using mental disciplines is for sure the better way, at least in order to divide (or even make some werewolf fight to your side with majesty) the pack or bring one of them straight in the trap ( with dominate: appear in front of him with obfuscate - obfuscate still works on other - and command him to go somewhere.).<br /> <br /> In a physical meaning, a Vampire, built for combat, can stands and even wins against a werewolf (of same experience at least). But she MUST be able to deal aggravated (unholy claws or, even better, feeding the crone). Having coil of the wyrm or/and ride the wave style is a great thing.<br /> Talking about the simple pools, they can be quite the same for the two races. The real problem is that a werewolf can heal ALL the damage reflexively at the start of each turn. So you can handle this dealing aggravated damages.<br /> <br /> EDIT: dealing aggravated in a grapple is a good chance for the vampire. The vamp pool for a grapple can be greater then a same experience garou.<br /> <br /> If you can't deal aggravated damage, a really good chance to win is: a great pool in the attack, the murder expert merit, and obfuscate 3. In that way you should be able to deal ALL the damage you need to kill the werewolf in the first attacks as automatic success (spent vitae in strenght and active vigor) and the werewolf can't even apply his defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-03-2016, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T05:04:29-08:00","id":799532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799513#post799513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a physical meaning, a Vampire, built for combat, can stands and even wins against a werewolf (of same experience at least). But she MUST be able to deal aggravated (unholy claws or, even better, feeding the crone). Having coil of the wyrm or/and ride the wave style is a great thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to disagree with this. A Rahu with high levels of Purity and Glory is going to generally have better dice pools than a vampire with high levels of Vigor and Resilience. And that's before we start touching on the whole host of merits, like Efficent Killer or Relentless Assult. <br /> <br /> If a wolf succeeds on a Hold Maneuver, then you might as well be dead with Efficent Killer in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-03-2016, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T05:20:03-08:00","id":799542,"title":"","content":"I didn't specificate during riding the wave or in frenzy. <br /> <br /> Why the pool for equal experience garou should be so much higher?<br /> There was a topic where were compared the pool of two top and same level character (vamp bp5 e equal werewolf with all the combat gift and merits). The result was that for claws the werewolf had 3 dice more in the pool but in grapple had lower dice pool. Using a grapple and winning the control let you deal aggravated damage with no defense reduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T05:51:45-08:00","id":799559,"title":"","content":"Its actually pretty neat how a each tactic would actually play out [ I have both Werewolf 2e and Vampire 2e open and side by side].<br /> <br /> Dominate &amp; Majesty are both very potent against pretty much anyone or anything, but Werewolves do have access to a few gifts that can resist the effects (Inspiration - <i>Fearless Hunter</i>) in addition to Supernatural Tolerance and Hunter's Aspect (which is the Werewolf Equivalent to Predatory Aura).<br /> <br /> Physical Disciplines are a must for any Vampire looking to physically engage a Werewolf. Outside of the limited-duration Gauru, <i>Urshul</i> will be the deadliest form a Werewolf can take, and a Vampire would need Celerity 2, Resilience 2, and Vigor 2 to match it (and additional edges granted by the disciplines off set some of the Werewolves inherent powers nicely). Please note that this is not counting any Gifts that the werewolf would also be using in a fight (and almost every Gift set contains a facet or two with direct combat application). I will echo earlier advice to double down on anything that deals aggravated damage, its the one thing that werewolves cannot easily counter, minimize, or negate.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate is probably the best point for point stealth power across the CofD gamelines.The only real counter available to a Werewolf is the Insight Gift <i>Scent the Unnatural</i>,but unless the Werewolf has reason to suspect lurking Vampires, it may not be activated. If the storyteller wants to increase the threat, they might let a Werewolf use Wolf Senses to initiate a Clash (I think this would be too much, but its not unreasonable). Obfuscate gives an edge in an Ambush (Add Obfuscate to the roll), but its still contested (by a creature with considerable sensory bonuses). If the ambush fails, Murder Expert won't come into play. <br /> <br /> Werewolves are vulnerable to the Kiss,but more resistant than regular mortals -The Vampire has to spend willpower to inflict Scarred or Swooning. It will be the storytellers call as to whether or not spending essence to offset lethal damage caused by feeding is considered &quot;resisting&quot;.<br /> <br /> Blood Addiction and Blood Bond work normally, but Supernaturals should be treated as Vampires for the purposes of resisting. It will be the storytellers call as to whether or not the Strength Gift <i>Unchained</i> lets the Uratha snap mental bindings the same way they can snap physical bindings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T06:14:48-08:00","id":799568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799239#post799239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that the Werewolves have Wolf-Blooded pack members and allies, have vampires target their enemy through them. The right mix of Dominate, Majesty, Vinculum, and Vitae Addiction should give the Kindred an edge. And that's not counting in the ghouls who can act in their stead during the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give an example of how to use these 'softer' targets to drive the Werewolves back, prevent them launching or succeeding at a Hunt targetingthe Vampires, etc.? These Vampires don't want these Werewolves next door and want them to leave, but will settle for some form of deal/oath between the groups that will keep the Werewolves away from Vampiric interests.<br /> <br /> In the second scenario (Werewolves have killed touchstones and Vampires want them dead) could you give an example of how to use the manipulated 'softer' targets to cause long term harm or death to the Werewolf?<br /> <br /> 'Target them through the less supernaturally potent members of the pack' is a starting point, but what is the scheme that gets to pushing the Werewolves away?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Tooth and Claw - </b>In Werewolf 2e, it is explicitly called out that the teeth of a werewolf in every form (including Hishu) deal supernatural damage. The claws soften a target up, bit Werewolves kill with their teeth. A Vampires resistance to mundane damage would protect them from a werewolves claws in most situations. I would make exceptions for when the Werewolf uses Gifts to augment their damage (such as Crushing Blow or Rending Claws), and for when the Werewolf has gone into <i>Basu-Im</i> (Death Rage). </div> </div> </div>Cool, biting = bad, clawing = simpler to deal with..but still bad. Does mean not getting caught up in grapples is important. What tools do Werewolves have for dealing with something in a non-solid form like Protean 5? I don't mean ghosts/spirits in Twilight (there's a gift I've seen for that as well as a Rite to force them to manifest).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Blood Sorcery</b> - Generally speaking, Vampire Magic focuses on channeling the Curse, and has limited capabilities to effect the Spirit world. A Vampire occultist would have to deal with ephemeral creatures using the methods and techniques available to mortal occultists [See Mortal Interaction in the Ephemeral Entities section of the appropriate books].<br /> While they have not been updated to 2e, the Circle of the Crone book has several rituals that explicitly interact with spirits ( pages.201-204) they are considered optional, since Spirit Magic is more of a Mage or Werewolf thing. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, going through the Themes now I've got my book to hand none mention Spirits or Ghosts directly. Divination can probably find them and Transmutation can probably force them to Manifest or maybe even change their nature at the highest levels. Creation high enough can make Silver and Destruction just makes very unpleasant things happen. Though would need to be Rank 5 to deal with Gauru/Kuruth otherwise it would pretty much bounce in that state. There's a pair of Crone and one could probably use their divination very frequently to just keep a constant heads up of risk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Shifting</b> - As of second edition, a Werewolf at most harmony levels ( 8 or less) shifts with them. Belongings in Dalu (Near Human) adjust to fit,but would be otherwise functional.Belongings in Gauru (Warform), Urshul (Near-Wolf) and Urhan (Wolf) are subsumed into the werewolves essence and become non-functional in all respects. So trying to track a werewolf by cellphone signal is a frustrating exercise where the signal vanishes seemingly at random. </div> </div> </div>Ok, seems the plan to use Majesty and the like to make some of the mortals and wolf-blooded get the pack at large to install and use 'find my phone' apps so the vampires would have a semi-real time 'minimap HUD' of the wolves would fall apart at some critical moments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>General Advice for Vampires</b><ul><li>Avoid head to head fight - unless you can secure a distinct tactical advantage. An individual Vampire warrior can be more than a match for a Uratha, but this represent a specialized skill set. Even a Werewolf accountant can turn into a killer at the drop of a hat. If the Vampires do not have access to reliable silver weapons, cannot marshal a force of their deadliest warriors, or cannot draft minions that won't lose their minds with Lunacy, try to use diplomacy or social attacks.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assume the Werewolves know this and realise they are under attack (they moved into the area knowing Vampires held it, they know there will be push back, they know Kindred strengths in general terms and know their Uratha strengths). The Werewolves are trying to force face to face encounters and their skills are pretty good at finding a target and stopping it escaping.<br /> <br /> What could the Kindred do to ensure they aren't being found - especially considering their daytime issues? Same for Vampire ghouls and key mortal pawns, how to keep them safe from determined Wolves trying to force a face to face encounter?<ul><li><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Know your Limits - I have run many a Vampire game where the group mystic wants to beat the Werewolves at their own game. This is almost always a mistake. Under the best of circumstances a Vampires spirit arsenal is limited vs a Werewolf who's entire arsenal IS spirit. Learn a trick or two, use it when needed, but for the most part don't invest heavily in this tactic. </div> </div> </div></li> </ul><br /> Any suggestions on how a Vampire could deal with a determined Rite master with Spirit allies spying, attacking from the Shadow and Twilight, etc.? An allied Fire spirit in Twilight hanging around the Kindred for example.<ul><li><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Use your strength - Vampires excel at influence, manipulation, and twisting mortal society around their fingers. Most Vampires have some investment in social merits (Allies, Contacts, Mentors, Retainers, Resources, Staff). Use these to counter and undermine The Werewolves resources. Use Disciplines, Bribery, Coercion and Extortion to undermine their non - Uratha and entirely mortal support base. Heck, use these resources against the Uratha themselves! Don't think of the Werewolves as invading Orcs, but as individuals. And every individual has a price. No other supernatural group is as invested in the structure of mortal society,and no other group can weapon that society as easily or as well. </div> </div> </div></li> </ul><br /> What are those key resources the Werewolves have in the world that they really need that the Kindred can attack and take from them? After speed reading the W:tF2e book I never really came away with the feeling that the Werewolves actually <i>care</i> that much about mortal society. They can fairly effectively live without it and can adopt an almost 'scorched earth' policy, losing homes, wealth, contacts and the like in the pursuit of the Hunt and rebuild after. Afterall, if they Hunt down and kill the Vampires they can rebuild their homes, wealth and contacts. I think there was even a tribe or lodge that was sort of about knowing when to discard resources for the Hunt.<br /> <br /> Let's say the Kindred get the police to have a valid search warrant on the Werewolves' home, they have mind-whammied one of the wolf-blooded to be hiding a large stash of drugs in the home. The Police find the drugs and want to arrest the Wolves. Why can't the Wolves just...leave and hole up somewhere else while they continue their Hunt? They don't, as far as I can see, actually <i>need</i> that home to be able to use their gifts or rites or forms to find the Kindred and tear them apart. Some of the fiction in the W:tF2e book has the Pack being hunted by the police but still going about and finding and killing the Rat-monster thing so...why not the same with Kindred?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the first issue here is that we're assuming a violent death spiral here. Vampires are the Social splat, whereas Wolves are the Physical. The vamps are best suited to win through non-physical means. Take a look at Dominate, Majesty, etc. Most start failing to work in combat. So stay out of it. Meet somewhere the wolves won't be eager to attack - or find someway to meet in relative safety. Once there, the vamps have the advantage socially. Vampire obfuscate is leagues better than Uratha stealth, and following one around is good, and most Insight Gifts are unsuited for calling for Clash of Wills here; yes, they could use Scent the Unnatural, but that costs Essence to activate, and the vampire is simply unnoticable, so little reason to activate it in the first place. Boundry Ward is probably the best detection method, but even that is questionable in this case. </div> </div> </div>I almost don't see how you can avoid the Death Spiral. If the Vampires are bing successful at the shutting down of the Pack through social means that's likely to start causing frustrations and tension and aggression amongst the group of almost hair trigger death rage monsters who have specific rites and culture about Sacred Hunts. As the Kindred start succeeding why <i>wouldn't</i> the Werewolves be pushed more and more towards <i>Siskur-Dah</i> on the Coterie? Once someone dies - a Touchstone for example or a mortal pack-member - what stops the escalation of violence that we see in things like Sunni/Shia fighting or Protestant/Catholic tit-for-tat in Northern Ireland and so on? Especially when the core of one side is barely contained death rage monsters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T06:19:21-08:00","id":799569,"title":"","content":"Talking about just numbers I think the situation is: (BP 5 for vamp. and equivalent for Werewolf...at greater BP the balance hangs for the vampire I suppose)<br /> <br /> (I took it from an old topic)<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Werewolf in Gauru attack pool:</b> 5 Str + 3 (Gauru) + 2 (Merits that increase Strength) + 10 (for Crimson Spasm - I made a roll with 18 dice and dobled the successes) + 5 (Gift of Strength) + 5 Brawl -1 (Relentless Assault to gain +1 damage) = 29 dice, with 8-again from Killer Instinct (1st dot Rahu Auspice Gift)<br /> <b>Werewolf in Gauru damage pool:</b> 2 (teeth) + 1 (relentless assualt) + 1 (living weapon) + 5 (slaughterer) = + 9 lethal <br /> <b>Werewolf Defense:</b> 9 (Dex/Wits + Athletics)<br /> <b>Werewolf Health:</b> 5 (size) + 5 (Stamina) + 4 (Gauru) + 1 (Favored Form) + 5 (Warrior's Hide - 2nd dot Rahu Auspice Gift) = 20<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire attack pool:</b> 5 Str + 5 (Frenzy) + 5 (Passive Vigor) + 6 (3 vitae) + 5 Brawl = 26 <br /> <b>Vampire damage pool:</b> +0 agg (claws of the unholy) + 5 (Active Vigor) = + 5 agg OR +2agg (feeding the Crone) + 5 (Active Vigor) = 7 agg<br /> <b>Vampire defense:</b> 9 (Gauru prevents you from adding any skill to defense so just Dex/Wits + Celerity) but with Coil of the Wyrm 4 add 5 for BP and rise defense to 14<br /> <b>Vampire Health:</b> 5 (size) + 5 (Stamina) + 5 (Resilience) + 5 BP (Coil of the wyrm 4) = 20<br /> <br /> I've ignored the Efficient Killer merit because I think the drawback (&quot;This Merit only works on living targets with discernible weak points&quot;) rules out Vampires (if there's something to contradict this I'd love to know).&quot;<br /> <br /> So the pools are 2-3 dice lower (the 8 again can be compensated from 5 more defense) and this not sound to me as an impossible match for the vamp.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T06:25:41-08:00","id":799571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799542#post799542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't specificate during riding the wave or in frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div> I assumed it when you brought up Wyrm and Ride the Wave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why the pool for equal experience garou should be so much higher? </div> </div> </div> Simple, really. For everything that a vampire can buy in terms of raising one's combat ability, there's an equivalent ability in Werewolf for about the same EXP cost. Raising Vigor increases your Strength and weapon damage rating. Purity raises your Health, your Strength, and auto-successes in combat, as well as gives you 8-again and inflict combat Tilts; at Purity 5, we have Crimson Spasm, which raises several important combat stats higher. Raising Reslience raises your Health and reduces damage taken, while Glory reduces damage taken. So far, in terms of raising Purity and Glory versus Vigor and Resilience, the Rahu is roughly equal to the combat vampire, with a few more tricks up his sleeve. Crimson Spasm means the wolf blows the vampire out of the water.<br /> <br /> Now, lets look at Riding the Wave merit. Five dots, and we're getting some nice bonuses to fighting, adding in willpower and BP. For the same five dots worth of merits, we can get Relentless Assult, which (when combined with spending willpower) raises the Rahu's combat ability by a roughly equal amount. Raise your vampire's BP by a dot for more power, both in terms of vitae spending and Riding the Wave benefits. The werewolf takes Fortified Form and Living Weapon. Riding the wave and spending one vitae (remembre we have to save some for Vigor and Resilence, so that's at least BP 3, we'll say) boosts a vampire's attack pool by +5. With Fortified Form, we've got 2/2 armor, which handily negates the boosted dice pool. With Living Weapon, we have +1 damage and ignore mundane armor, which means that our wolf's bite damgae just got that much worse. The werewolf is absolutely at an advantage right now.<br /> <br /> The vampire joins the Ordo and learns Coil of the Wyrm. You need four dots before it starts adding into combat ability, for 16 EXP, for +BP to Defense, Health, and Speed. The Werewolf buys up PU and Favored Form, which gives him lots of exceptional successes in combat, raises his Strength more. This puts the vampire roughly back on par with the Rahu.<br /> <br /> We've spent a lot of EXP in the most efficent way here. Now, that's a lot of EXP so far. The vampire can raise his BP to get more advatnages over the wolf, yes. But the wolf is still getting more dice/armor from Crimson Spasm which puts him firmly in powerhouse territory, is inflicting Tilts that the vampire needs to heal (reducing the vamp's attack pools), getting exceptional successes all over the place (two actions during grapples), and can attack/grapple in the same action. That neatly offsets any advantage the vampire might have had, and getting grappled by the wolf means that he's dead when Efficent Killer comes into play.<br /> <br /> All this is assuming the vampire has enough vitae to keep fighting as well. Vampires have limited vitae pools to power all these attacks - they nova, then whimper. A werewolf in Kuruth uses all these abilities without cost (except Crimson Spasm, which is just 1 essence a turn). That means the vampire needs to build up a good Herd and Location if he's expecting to have enough blood to do anything worthwhile. The werewolf is happy at being essence efficent, and will instead channel those EXP into other abilities. Or fetishes, which open up entirely new avenues. <br /> <br /> The vampire can try to use silver weapons, but that can be disarmed through lots of means - arm wrecking, grapple, etc. The vampire can aim to purchase Protean and Cruac for agg damage, but that is more EXP sunk into a situation that lets the werewolf get more varied Gifts and abilties, keeping him abreast, if not ahead. And still doesn't solve the Efficent Killer problem. Or a werewolf using Element (fire). <br /> <br /> Eventually, at very high levels of BP and support structures, our unrealistic combat munchkins turn towards the vampire with the advantage for the handful of rounds he's got the vitae for. I don't know if its enough to kill the wolf before the vamp runs out of steam, and frankly, it doesn't matter, because we're talking unrealistc amounts of EXP that I never expect to see happen, and all channeled towards combat twinkery. <br /> <br /> <br /> TL;DR - Anything that a vampire does to raise his combat potential, the werewolf has an equal or better ability they can buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T06:54:15-08:00","id":799577,"title":"","content":"In addition to the many things already mentioned:<br /> <br /> 1)<b> Auspex + Obfuscate</b>: This allows you to quickly find the weak spots and breaking points. Once the Mekhet has scouted the situation, it is up to the Daeva and Ventrue to ruin the werewolves lives... or at least threaten to.<br /> <br /> 2) <b>Social versus Social</b>: It is true that werewolves have many Gifts that help them mobilise social assets too, but they cannot match the ease with which vampires do it. Lupines get bonuses to Social Maneuvering, vampires just straight up make you do shit or love them. Every member of the extended pack is a possible weak spot, only a bit of Dominate, Majesty or drop of Vitae from being turned around. Of course, you have to be hard and decisive. Chances are, the Totem is going to notice shenanigans.<br /> <br /> 3) <b>Ghoul pawns</b>: Vampires create thralls and good cannon fodder like no other splat. Ghouls are relatively cheap to make and decently effective force. Lunacy is an issue, but can possibly be dealt with through numbers or supernatural force (I guess it is up to the ST whether Majesty or Dominate can Clash of Wills against Lunacy or maybe just straight up ignore it).<br /> <br /> 4) <b>Fuck up their territory: </b>Use your mortal connections to have the police start investigations, politican passing demolition of buildings important to the pack, mafia shenanigans on their turf. If you do not have the Social Merits, force the issue with Disciplines and the Vinculum.<br /> <br /> 5) <b>The Pure/Forsaken</b>: You say the Pack is new? Do the PCs know any established packs or know Ancillae and Elders that might know some? Sic'em on them! Promise rewards and concessions and let the wolfies deal with it themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> If it comes to a relatively even physical clash (which the Kindred should avoid, as pointed out by other posters), the biggest advantages vampires have are probably:<br /> <br /> 1) <b>Burst Damage and Focused Attacks</b>: When comparing vampire and werewolf healing and damage mitigation, it becomes clear that werewolves are better at drawn out fights. Their basic Lethal Damage healing is at least equal or even more efficient than Vitae healing, point-per-point, depending on their Primal Urge. However, a vampire is only limited by their Vitae-per-turn while a Lupine has a fixed limit of how much they can heal in a turn even with Essence, unless they go Garou. Resilience also means a vampire can be supremely tough to take down except through extreme burst damage from single attacks. A Garou werewolf, meanwhile, can suffer a death of a thousand cuts once you pile on enough damage in a turn. That is if the fight even lasts that long. Ideally, weaponry, Celerity, Vigor, Obfuscate and even Cr\u00faac (<i>Touch of the Morrigan</i>, <i>Feeding the Crone</i>) would be used to drop a werewolf before they can Death Rage. Of course, achieving better combat coordination than a pack of lupines could be tricky...<br /> <br /> 2) <b>Bane versus Bane</b>: Silver is a somewhat easier weapon to wield than fire. The Kindred should have Social Merits that allow them to get their hands on silver weaponry and ammunition, which can then be wielded like any gun or blade. If normal channels fail, getting a Theban Sorcerer to do some transmutation can help. Meanwhile, a flamethrower is hard to get, molotov cocktails are extremely finite and require preperation and torches make for awkward weapons. Not to mention once they go <i>kuruth </i>they will likely not have the faculties to use those anymore. The worst case for the Kindred would be if the werewolves have befriended/enslaved a fire spirit, but those do not exactly grow on trees. The ol' hairspray-lighter combo also works of course. Even then, though, Resilience helps a lot and I do not (correct me if I am wrong) remember a Gift that downgraded/reduced damage from silver.<br /> <br /> 3) <b>Nightmare</b>: Holy shit, Nightmare. This likely will not be an option since you did not mention a Nosferatu, but dayum. <i>Face of the Beast</i> (NIghtmare 2) and someone is either out of the fight or hemmorhaging Willpower like crazy. The ST should be clear on how exactly this power works on lupines though. It might require you to be careful about not ending up in the path of a panicking lupine in <i>kuruth </i>trying to get away.<br /> <br /> 4) <b>Going on the Offence: </b>Yes, this contradicts what was said above, including by myself. But if you have to deal with them violently, try to hit them first. The biggest advantage of werewolves is not <i>kuruth, </i>but being on the Hunt. Kill them before they hunt you down. This also can give you the chance to make full use of focused burst damage (as described above).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 01-03-2016, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:07:11-08:00","id":799585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799571#post799571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I assumed it when you brought up Wyrm and Ride the Wave.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, lets look at Riding the Wave merit. Five dots, and we're getting some nice bonuses to fighting, adding in willpower and BP. For the same five dots worth of merits, we can get Relentless Assult, which (when combined with spending willpower) raises the Rahu's combat ability by a roughly equal amount. Raise your vampire's BP by a dot for more power, both in terms of vitae spending and Riding the Wave benefits. The werewolf takes Fortified Form and Living Weapon. Riding the wave and spending one vitae (remembre we have to save some for Vigor and Resilence, so that's at least BP 3, we'll say) boosts a vampire's attack pool by +5. With Fortified Form, we've got 2/2 armor, which handily negates the boosted dice pool. With Living Weapon, we have +1 damage and ignore mundane armor, which means that our wolf's bite damgae just got that much worse. The werewolf is absolutely at an advantage right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember, Crismons gives just ONE of the presented benefits at turn (or more dice pool or armor or health), and Unholy Claws ngore armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799571#post799571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We've spent a lot of EXP in the most efficent way here. Now, that's a lot of EXP so far. The vampire can raise his BP to get more advatnages over the wolf, yes. But the wolf is still getting more dice/armor from Crimson Spasm which puts him firmly in powerhouse territory, is inflicting Tilts that the vampire needs to heal (reducing the vamp's attack pools), getting exceptional successes all over the place (two actions during grapples), and can attack/grapple in the same action. That neatly offsets any advantage the vampire might have had, and getting grappled by the wolf means that he's dead when Efficent Killer comes into play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always if I remember right, the gift (or wathever it was) that inflicts tilts can be used only when garou is facing more than one enemy at time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799571#post799571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Eventually, at very high levels of BP and support structures, our unrealistic combat munchkins turn towards the vampire with the advantage for the handful of rounds he's got the vitae for. I don't know if its enough to kill the wolf before the vamp runs out of steam, and frankly, it doesn't matter, because we're talking unrealistc amounts of EXP that I never expect to see happen, and all channeled towards combat twinkery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I know it's unrealistic amount of experience. But in order to considere the potentiality of each race we have to consider the top of both. Cause in a realistic situation, the victory depends on the particular build of each contender <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, like I said, it's not a duel that can last for long time. It should finish in two or three turns or the vamp would have not chance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-03-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:13:45-08:00","id":799588,"title":"","content":"The issue with using Face of the Beast on a werewolf is that in Kuruth they lose the ability to tell friend from foe. If they can't identify their friends, how are they supposed to identify the thing they're scared of? <br /> <br /> Basically in their head it would go something like this: WHERE'S THE SCARY THING GONE? FUCK IT, MURDER EVERYTHING!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:15:49-08:00","id":799589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799588#post799588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with using Face of the Beast on a werewolf is that in Kuruth they lose the ability to tell friend from foe. If they can't identify their friends, how are they supposed to identify the thing they're scared of?<br /> <br /> Basically in their head it would go something like this: WHERE'S THE SCARY THING GONE? FUCK IT, MURDER EVERYTHING!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I'm not wrong, face of the beast works also in a unconscious way. The victim feel an indefinite terror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:18:43-08:00","id":799591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799568#post799568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you give an example of how to use these 'softer' targets to drive the Werewolves back, prevent them launching or succeeding at a Hunt targetingthe Vampires, etc.? These Vampires don't want these Werewolves next door and want them to leave, but will settle for some form of deal/oath between the groups that will keep the Werewolves away from Vampiric interests.<br /> <br /> In the second scenario (Werewolves have killed touchstones and Vampires want them dead) could you give an example of how to use the manipulated 'softer' targets to cause long term harm or death to the Werewolf?<br /> <br /> 'Target them through the less supernaturally potent members of the pack' is a starting point, but what is the scheme that gets to pushing the Werewolves away?</div> </div> </div> </div> Suicide bombers, getting information, poisoning the pack, selling out to rival packs for advatnage. There's several ways you can leverage this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cool, biting = bad, clawing = simpler to deal with..but still bad. Does mean not getting caught up in grapples is important. What tools do Werewolves have for dealing with something in a non-solid form like Protean 5? I don't mean ghosts/spirits in Twilight (there's a gift I've seen for that as well as a Rite to force them to manifest). </div> </div> </div> Protean swarm form and mist forms are actually pretty powerful advatnages on the vampire side. However, I think Gifts of the Elements or some other nature-power might work against the vampire in this case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What could the Kindred do to ensure they aren't being found - especially considering their daytime issues? Same for Vampire ghouls and key mortal pawns, how to keep them safe from determined Wolves trying to force a face to face encounter? </div> </div> </div> Not much can escape a werewolf hunting. Wolves literally have a power to track you by where your shadow has been. The best thing that vampires can do is just get in a car, get distance, and plan an encounter somewhere they have the advantage. Tracking on two/four feet takes time. Harrass the wolves through police, so that they can regain initiative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any suggestions on how a Vampire could deal with a determined Rite master with Spirit allies spying, attacking from the Shadow and Twilight, etc.? An allied Fire spirit in Twilight hanging around the Kindred for example. </div> </div> </div> Spirits need essence, so there's limited number of abilities they can use, and won't go somewhere too far from their fetters. Reaching is very costly, and having powerful abilities is reserved for more powerful spirits, who demand much in return for their services. The best defense is making sure the ST plays the spirits intellegently. Also, perform an abjuration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are those key resources the Werewolves have in the world that they really need that the Kindred can attack and take from them? </div> </div> </div> Their pack. Werewolves aren't psychopaths, they have friends and family. Many Iron Masters end up with lots of contacts and allies, or even join the poilice department. The wolves are very territorial, so wll have buildings and neighborhoods they want to maintain and control, which includes people. <br /> <br /> And then, there's the locus. Wreewolves need essence, and maintaining a locus is critically important. Not only for their own reserves, but for their spirit allies that this pack is theoretically hiring out as spies and attackers. Abandoning a locus is a huge blow to the Uratha, larger than forcing a vampire out of its feeding grounds. Vampires can feed anywhere. Werewolves need that essence to maintain spirit allies. Otherwise, they have to spend lots of time hunting spirits in the Hisil, and who has time for that? The wolves could also eat people, but that would eventually trap them in the Hisil as well, making it a losing proposition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After speed reading the W:tF2e book I never really came away with the feeling that the Werewolves actually <i>care</i> that much about mortal society. They can fairly effectively live without it and can adopt an almost 'scorched earth' policy, losing homes, wealth, contacts and the like in the pursuit of the Hunt and rebuild after. Afterall, if they Hunt down and kill the Vampires they can rebuild their homes, wealth and contacts. I think there was even a tribe or lodge that was sort of about knowing when to discard resources for the Hunt. </div> </div> </div>Scorched earth policies are very good ways of creating Wounds. Forsaken want to maintain the Hisil/Flesh balance, and the Pure have spirit gods they want to follow, forcing certain resonance. Unless your werewolves are demented, no one wants that much bad spiritual resonance in the area. Spirits of destruction are not easy to get rid of. <br /> <br /> And there's very good chance that you can't &quot;simply rebuild&quot; after scorching it. Losing your Contacts can lead to them refusing to talk to you ever again, which means that long term hunting is difficult. Losing your home can raise the eyebrows of insurance companies, who mark the wolves for arson investigations. <br /> <br /> And, of course, there's the fear of hunters as well. Going Garau in front of witnesses leads to wolf bloods. Wolf blood can become hunters immune to lunacy. Werewolves need to hide from humans as much as vampires do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I almost don't see how you can avoid the Death Spiral. If the Vampires are bing successful at the shutting down of the Pack through social means that's likely to start causing frustrations and tension and aggression amongst the group of almost hair trigger death rage monsters who have specific rites and culture about Sacred Hunts. </div> </div> </div> First, its a false cliche that vampires only work through Allies and other social contacts. Yes, the Invictus and Movement specialize in it, and their Masquerade counterparts encourage this cliche, but that's only two of five covenants in Requiem. An Ordo Dracul with Coil of the Vovoid, for instance, would rely on bloodbonds instead, inflicting a full Vinculum when the wolf bites him in combat. The Lance and Circle would use their rituals to mess with the wolves instead of social groups. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a Daeva that approaches the wolves in a crowded space can Majesty the entire group, assuming they're not willing to Garou out in public. Even if one of the wolves had Fearless Hunter, it won't protect the pack as a whole. Fearless Hunter protects against the whole pack area-based influnces; Awe is a wide area, but its uncontested. Confidant, Green Eyes, and Loyalty are all single targets. So, if we assume that a wolf has Fearless Hunter (doubtful, if this group is as honorless as you imply; FH is an Honor based Gift) and does succeed against Confidant (again, its doubtful, since the vampire will still likely ahve a higher dice pool than the wolf), that's still a bunch of other wolves that don't stand a chance. Confidant has no cost, so it can be used repeatedly in rapid fire succession. Once the wolves have been Charmed, they won't want to attack the vampire. However, the vampire can use Green Eyes to send them on suicidal missions. Or a group orgy that ends up with all their blood drained, or under full vinculum plus addicted to the Kiss. A single vampire, in the right situation, can shut down an entire pack, and that's as a starting character. Imagine if we had Loyalty and Idol as well? Backup ghouls and cotorie mates? <br /> <br /> <br /> The problem here is that your theoretical vampires are letting the wolves play to their strength - predators hunting their prey. The vampires need to shift the confrontation to some arena where they have the advantage. Werewolves are built to hunt down their prey, slowly wearing down their strength. Vampires are built for shocks of speed and direct confrontation and social maneuvering; even powerful Xanatos Gambit elders manipulate through moving their empowered pawns, who use their rather direct abilities. This picking at each other is just something that wolves specialize in. That's not how vampires hunt at all. Death spiraling is playing to werewolf strength, not vampire strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:20:55-08:00","id":799592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799589#post799589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If I'm not wrong, face of the beast works also in a unconscious way. The victim feel an indefinite terror.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;OH GOD IT'S EVERYWHERE! MURDER EVERYTHING!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:20:57-08:00","id":799593,"title":"","content":"Interestingly that's where Obfuscate and Nightmare 1 come into play.<br /> <br /> Get the wolf into Kuruth, Obfuscate out of sight and start throwing those threatening and fearful illusions (that don't have an opposed roll) to try and steer the wolf toward or away from certain targets.<br /> <br /> Though the Hunter's Aspect having a considerably better dicepool (3 stats vs 2) that Predatory Aura probably means they'd break free of Nightmare 1 anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) <b>Fuck up their territory: </b>Use your mortal connections to have the police start investigations, politican passing demolition of buildings important to the pack, mafia shenanigans on their turf. If you do not have the Social Merits, force the issue with Disciplines and the Vinculum. </div> </div> </div>Why does this matter? Ultimately the more of this the Kindred do you start getting into human behaviour and desire for revenge. You take their home, their children's school, their blood-brother's place of work everything away form them and they just leave and stop attacking the Kindred? If anything doing this seems <i>more</i> likely to lead to a Sacred Hunt being called and forcing that face to face encounter that Werewolves are much better equipped to win than any general Kindred is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:24:51-08:00","id":799595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799577#post799577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to the many things already mentioned:<br /> <br /> <br /> If it comes to a relatively even physical clash (which the Kindred should avoid, as pointed out by other posters), the biggest advantages vampires have are probably:<br /> <br /> 1) <b>Burst Damage and Focused Attacks</b>: When comparing vampire and werewolf healing and damage mitigation, it becomes clear that werewolves are better at drawn out fights. Their basic Lethal Damage healing is at least equal or even more efficient than Vitae healing, point-per-point, depending on their Primal Urge. However, a vampire is only limited by their Vitae-per-turn while a Lupine has a fixed limit of how much they can heal in a turn even with Essence, unless they go Garou. Resilience also means a vampire can be supremely tough to take down except through extreme burst damage from single attacks. A Garou werewolf, meanwhile, can suffer a death of a thousand cuts once you pile on enough damage in a turn. That is if the fight even lasts that long. Ideally, weaponry, Celerity, Vigor, Obfuscate and even Cr\u00faac (<i>Touch of the Morrigan</i>, <i>Feeding the Crone</i>) would be used to drop a werewolf before they can Death Rage. Of course, achieving better combat coordination than a pack of lupines could be tricky...</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves have the best healing factor in garou, in other forms he sucks rising the blood potency <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799577#post799577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) <b>Nightmare</b>: Holy shit, Nightmare. This likely will not be an option since you did not mention a Nosferatu, but dayum. <i>Face of the Beast</i> (NIghtmare 2) and someone is either out of the fight or hemmorhaging Willpower like crazy. The ST should be clear on how exactly this power works on lupines though. It might require you to be careful about not ending up in the path of a panicking lupine in <i>kuruth </i>trying to get away.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. Furthemore you can use majesty or Dominate even in combat. With majesty you could thrall a werewolf and let him fight for you for several night. With Dominate you can make him run away or protect you untill he suffers more then stamina in lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799577#post799577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) <b>Going on the Offence: </b>Yes, this contradicts what was said above, including by myself. But if you have to deal with them violently, try to hit them first. The biggest advantage of werewolves is not <i>kuruth, </i>but being on the Hunt. Kill them before they hunt you down. This also can give you the chance to make full use of focused burst damage (as described above).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the point is that you should be able to take down a werewolf in two or three turns. The best way is. Obfuscate 3, murder expert dealing a killing blow (possibly with agg. damage).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-03-2016, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:31:58-08:00","id":799598,"title":"","content":"What exactly is the conflict between the vampires and the Uratha to begin with? It's rare that they would compete over hunting grounds, assuming the coterie isn't a Crone spirit cult that allows spirits to piggyback on their Herd for kicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:34:14-08:00","id":799600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799593#post799593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does this matter? Ultimately the more of this the Kindred do you start getting into human behaviour and desire for revenge. You take their home, their children's school, their blood-brother's place of work everything away form them and they just leave and stop attacking the Kindred? If anything doing this seems <i>more</i> likely to lead to a Sacred Hunt being called and forcing that face to face encounter that Werewolves are much better equipped to win than any general Kindred is.</div> </div> </div> </div> Several reasons. 1) several gifts are terriroty based. 2) Locus. 3) Spirit allies are territory based. Being driven from your territory does hurt werewolf strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799585#post799585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember, Crismons gives just ONE of the presented benefits at turn (or more dice pool or armor or health), and Unholy Claws ngore armor.</div> </div> </div> </div> You do not remember. Its one benefit per success, with repeats possible, and they last for one turn per essence spent. Technically, the book does say &quot;all armor not generated by Resilence.&quot; Resilence doesn't create armor, no does the powers I'm talking about except the merit, and since the merit is magical, its arguable that an ST would allow it. And my initial analysis didn't include claws - protean came later. If you use CotU, you're actually doing less damage than if you use a silver axe. That +0 modifier hurts your damage output a lot, and the Glory Rage gift will shrug off the damage like nothing else.<br /> And we're talking about a pack of vampires. Alternatively, we can also get a fetish that removes that restiction. The Savage Rending applies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes I know it's unrealistic amount of experience. But in order to considere the potentiality of each race we have to consider the top of both. </div> </div> </div> If you have to use theoretical elders and nothing approaching what a PC might have, your conclusions for what the vampire PCs in this situation should do are highly flawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-03-2016, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:47:33-08:00","id":799605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799588#post799588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically in their head it would go something like this: WHERE'S THE SCARY THING GONE? FUCK IT, MURDER EVERYTHING!</div> </div> </div> </div>Which could be just as well, if the vampires react right. But yeah, it realy depends on how the ST rules that power interacts with werewolf nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T07:52:58-08:00","id":799607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799600#post799600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Several reasons. 1) several gifts are terriroty based. 2) Locus. 3) Spirit allies are territory based. Being driven from your territory does hurt werewolf strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest issue I have is that I've run and played Vampire for quite a while so know first hand what kinds of things PCs (and by extension, Kindred) care about, how they scheme and plan and respond. I have no experience with W:tF (which is changing soonish) so don't know the realities of how they act or respond, how they scheme or combine their abilities, what kinds of things they care about and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have to use theoretical elders and nothing approaching what a PC might have, your conclusions for what the vampire PCs in this situation should do are highly flawed. </div> </div> </div>Yes, theoretical hundred XP types are - while certainly interesting thought exercises - less useful than what might be done by broadly (as in, not purely combat) built characters with 10-25xp.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T08:01:16-08:00","id":799612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799592#post799592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;OH GOD IT'S EVERYWHERE! MURDER EVERYTHING!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes actually your interpretation could be right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T08:13:33-08:00","id":799618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799593#post799593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does this matter? Ultimately the more of this the Kindred do you start getting into human behaviour and desire for revenge. You take their home, their children's school, their blood-brother's place of work everything away form them and they just leave and stop attacking the Kindred? If anything doing this seems <i>more</i> likely to lead to a Sacred Hunt being called and forcing that face to face encounter that Werewolves are much better equipped to win than any general Kindred is.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what MCN said:<br /> <br /> 1) It takes away some of their advantages when they do go on the Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> 2) Opens them up for a pre-emptive strike (whether by the PC or pawns).<br /> <br /> 3) Busies them with these mortal problems. Sure, they could ignore them, but in a realistic situation, people try to avoid pyrrhic victories and MAD.<br /> <br /> 4) Reveals more weaknesses that can be targeted more directly. Imagine the werewolf checking up on a loved one and then said love one shanks them with a silver dagger, a vacant expression on her face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T08:18:58-08:00","id":799624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799607#post799607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the biggest issue I have is that I've run and played Vampire for quite a while so know first hand what kinds of things PCs (and by extension, Kindred) care about, how they scheme and plan and respond. I have no experience with W:tF (which is changing soonish) so don't know the realities of how they act or respond, how they scheme or combine their abilities, what kinds of things they care about and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div> In general, werewolves hunt. Everything that werewolves do revolves around hunting, its their main strength. They need to maintain hunting grounds, they care about their pack, they are master shapeshifters. If it revolves around one of those four things, chances are that a werewolf can do it, and be better than any other supernatural at it. Hunting, territory, pack, shapeshifting. <br /> <br /> Rahu are the warriors - they hunt on battlefields. Irraka are the stealthy types - stalkers and assassins. Itheur are the shamans, who hunt down and bind spirits. Elodoth are the social face of the pack, the envoy, the judge, the one who plays politics and knows the red tape and connections to get things done. The Cahalith are... well, they're glorified bards - they're part socialite, part pack caretender, who coordinates and strengthens the pack on the hunt; jacks of all trades. Much like the D&amp;D party that the five Auspice kinda reflect, these five play off each other, each filling a different need and tactic in the hunt for their prey in different ways. Packs are designed to work with each other, and play off each other's strengths. Each has a role that they are called to fulfill, and are encouraged to act within it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T08:28:19-08:00","id":799631,"title":"","content":"My solution would be to go kill a couple of cops and then proceed to use mental Disciplines to make witnesses think it was one or more of the werewolves who did it. Let the human government take care of them. Them fighting back would only add more fuel to the fire and make things harder and harder on themselves until they're simply overwhelmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T09:16:43-08:00","id":799655,"title":"","content":"Does you Ventrue have Dominate 3? Because programed commands can be a huge boon. You'd only need to grab a pack member or two and give them commands like &quot;pour these silver flakes into the pack's next meal&quot; or &quot;place this satchel charge under the Alpha's bed tonight&quot;. Perhaps even permit &quot;Go into Kuruth tonight at the pack congregation&quot;<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 3 or 4 could achieve similar results, assuming the pack doesn't have some form of ward to warn them when you've entered. Walk in, poison the well (figuratively speaking) and walk back out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T09:22:23-08:00","id":799659,"title":"","content":"I agree with the cops thing. The most important thing is to never meet them face to face if you can avoid it.<br /> <br /> Because they can track by scent, Hunters in Darkness can locate all your safe places just by looking at you, an Uratha with Know Thy Prey can identify all your allies, contacts and other social merits just by looking at you, and an Elodoth can identify any lie you tell them face to face<br /> <br /> As far as obfuscate, they can track you via Impossible Spoor (triggering a clash of will at least), and Boundary Ward can prevent you ever getting the drop on them in their den. Lore of the Land will outright reveal you if you are nearby. If they have Pack Awareness it makes it even harder to surprise one without alerting all the others. Similarly, if you fail to surprise one, you fail to surprise all the one with Pack Awareness. Fearless Predator means that if you fail to Dominate or Majesty one, they all resist. Together they are strong. <br /> <br /> The best options are to split them up. Like Ashenrogue said, get one of them detained by Police for questioning. Frame them for a crime and have the police keep them for questioning or in Jail overnight (a Saturday night arrest sometimes means you spend the weekend in Jail in some small towns until court opens up on Monday to process you). The important thing again, is to never have it link back to your coterie. While there, you can give them water with one of your vampire's blood in it - get some viniculum going. <br /> <br /> Turn them against each other. Let the police come asking for one of the others, as though the detained one broke under pressure. Make up lies. Find out where they spend time separately and force them to spend more time there alone. You have to take them down one by one. The thing is, killing one is going to get the rest banding together to find the threat, so the best thing to do is to let there appear to be no threat for as long as you can. Take out one or two in separate coordinated strikes, get one or two under viniculum. Either way they are much weaker as a pack without one of their auspices. Of course with Read the World's Loom they might be able to divine vampire involvement, it's still helpful.<br /> <br /> You can also just turn the city on them, calling a citywide manhunt. Make the territory too hot for them. Turn the gangs against them, get their faces on the news, turn the people against them. Force them underground then find where they are underground and get that info out too. They can't fight the territory. Taking their territory from them is definitely a victory against werewolves.<br /> <br /> If you're eventually gonna fight, then taking one or two down first is your best option.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T09:32:06-08:00","id":799670,"title":"","content":"Although one should bear in mind that if need be, werewolves can retreat to a place no mortal can follow. Think you've driven them out? They could be watching you from the other side of the gauntlet <i>right now.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T09:39:56-08:00","id":799671,"title":"","content":"Very good point, honestly. It's pretty hard to take out a pack entrenched in their territory.<br /> <br /> When/if you do end up fighting, you definitely want to lure them out of their territory to somewhere they don't have knowledge of local/dedicated loci or relationships with local spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:18:36-08:00","id":799688,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd mostly just have the vampires recruit some disposable thugs, ghoul them, get them loaded with silver and then sic them on the pack while they least expect it. There are even a ton of ways it can be done without endangering the ghouls, such as drive-by shootings, sniping, planting bombs, etc. All the vampires need is to spend several nights planning and preparing. Attacking all the werewolves at the same time, before they can gather their bearings, should get rid of most of the pack. And after that? Well, send the ghouls to finish the stragglers off, perhaps sending the Gangrel as backup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T11:20:13-08:00","id":799713,"title":"","content":"You think sneaking into the heart of a werewolf pack's territory with a bomb isn't dangerous? They have ways of detecting intruders, y'know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T11:25:59-08:00","id":799714,"title":"","content":"The werewolves are, as per the OP, claiming territory in a place that is also a vampire's feeding grounds. This means there are a good amount of mortals already present in the territory. Therefore, the vampires can ghoul people either within that territory (which they should know fairly well, since it used to be their feeding grounds) or who must leave their territory semi-frequently (due to work, school, hobbies, etc.). If the ghoul already lives or frequently dwells in that territory, it's going to be very hard for the werewolves to realise something is amiss before the big strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T11:51:05-08:00","id":799721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799714#post799714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The werewolves are, as per the OP, claiming territory in a place that is also a vampire's feeding grounds. This means there are a good amount of mortals already present in the territory. Therefore, the vampires can ghoul people either within that territory (which they should know fairly well, since it used to be their feeding grounds) or who must leave their territory semi-frequently (due to work, school, hobbies, etc.). If the ghoul already lives or frequently dwells in that territory, it's going to be very hard for the werewolves to realise something is amiss before the big strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to disagree there. Detecting things that are amiss in their territories is one of werewolves' greatest strengths. Especially if they have any Hunters in Darkness or Iron Masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T11:56:58-08:00","id":799723,"title":"","content":"Unless werewolves have a specific &quot;Detect Hostile Intent&quot; effect that is both AoE throughout the entire territory and either is ongoing or they're paranoid enough to cast 24/7, I can't imagine how they're going to figure out that Randy McRandomPerson is planning to kill them, when they might not even <i>meet</i> that dude until he carries out his plans. If the territory is several blocks in a city, that's hundreds of people that live there and thousands that pass through it every day. The vampires can even just play it safe and ghoul people that live outside the territory but pass through it daily, to further throw off the werewolves' trails.<br /> <br /> Humans can't possibly be powerless to strike back at werewolves who've claimed their home as their territory. Hunter proves that your average group of humans has what it takes to take out a pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T12:50:04-08:00","id":799751,"title":"","content":"Read the World's Loom works as such:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Uratha gains insight from his surroundings, hearing of a coming threat from the growling engines of a traffic jam, reading secrets from amidst the gang tags on the <br /> walls, or seeing the sorry state of the Gauntlet in the patterns of scurrying cockroaches. The character learns of a single event, threat, or circumstance of meaningful relevance to the Uratha <br /> within his Glory Renown in miles. &quot;<br /> <br /> Things he can learn about<b></b>:<ul><li>Threats. (The police chief is planning a raid on the pack; werewolves come seeking a showdown; the tenement is unstable and will soon collapse; the old spirit Thurizag has returned)</li> <li>The supernatural. (Something preys on human residents in the area; something dwells in the high-rise; something numbs the minds of residents)</li> <li>Violence. (A riot is brewing; there is a pattern to the murders; a hunt is taking place)</li> <li>Conflicts. (Gangs are feuding over drug territory; the big corporation is under financial attack, the mayoral election is turning nasty)</li> </ul><br /> And if they pick up the scent of even one ghoul they have a whole host of other things they can do to determine threats.<br /> <br /> I mean you're right though, the trick is to prepare without their noticing and conduct a coordinated strike before they . But honestly, due to Down and Dirty fighting, a pack of werewolves and 3 turns of Garou can probably take down 50 people. Possibly even 20 ghouls depending on ST rulings. You ghoul more people than that and you're bound to get noticed eventually.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T12:58:06-08:00","id":799759,"title":"","content":"You could feasibly confuse Read the World's Loom by coordinating several simultaneous strikes using as wildly different resources/assets as possible. Have a riot happening at the same time as the police go for the werewolves at the same time as a dominated human detonates a bomb at the same time as a group of silver-bearing armed thugs gun down the werewolves, and so on. All the vampires need to do is grab a toy, wind it up and then let it go, aiming it at the werewolves. It's the werewolves who have to anticipate and counter several threats coming from different angles and using different methods.<br /> <br /> Now granted, if all those methods fail, then yes, the werewolves will have caught the scent/additional data of who was behind the murder attempts, and shit is likely to go down for the vamps. But doesn't that make for an interesting story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T14:11:18-08:00","id":799791,"title":"","content":"But knowing the Wolves can do that requires fairly intimate knowledge of the specific powers they wield. Setting up several overlapping threats that all only become threatening enough to be picked up by the loom within the same 24 hour span (and the user can reuse the gift asking for different info each time if they have the essence to pay for it) is fairly tricky additional work to be doing without knowing you'd need to. I could see sending on some thugs or dropping off the explosives/weapons/etc. in one location on one day in preparation for the coordinated attack taking place in two days time being foiled because the weapons stash triggers earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T14:17:43-08:00","id":799794,"title":"","content":"Knowing what werewolves are capable of sounds like an extended Intelligence+Occult check to me. Surely if the Mekhet is not up to the task, there may be some ally they can call to make the check for them. That should forewarn the vampires of what the werewolves can or can't do. From then on, it's up to the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T14:28:00-08:00","id":799800,"title":"","content":"The use of mind magic on the werewolves in question, if they're in <i>Kuruth</i>, also suffers twice the werewolf's Primal Urge as a penalty. That's at a minimum a -2 in addition to Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> I have more detailed answers to the OP's questions, but it'll have to wait a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T14:38:30-08:00","id":799805,"title":"","content":"I don't know about that, with a heavy penalty at best. I might even rule that you'd need to have a specialty in Werewolves to have knowledge of specific Facets (or a werewolf contact/specialist). Splats tend to keep their secrets pretty close to the vest for just that reason. That's fairly specific knowledge.<br /> <br /> Though if you want to GM fiat it to give your players an edge, you might be better off just not giving the werewolves that facet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T15:07:08-08:00","id":799823,"title":"","content":"I've only read the first post so forgive me if this is outdated.<br /> <br /> Really, diplomacy is the way to deal with the threat. Unless the town is exceptionally small, a pack of vampires and werewolves should be able to share it. Even then, they both want different things. Vampires need blood, werewolves need Essence. Unless the werewolves are outright man-eaters, or there's no loci, they aren't really likely to be fighting over domains. And if there are no loci, the werewolves would probably be better served by finding some other place to reside. It's worth pointing out that werewolves can make loci, so even if the vampires all happen to lair in the same place, which is also the only locus in town, the werewolves can make a more conveniently accessed locus on their own. Slaughtering a bunch of undead and having them fuel their blood magics in a battle over a locus is likely to taint the locus, or at least spawn rival spirits.<br /> <br /> After things have escalated, the vampires are likely to lose in a straight up fight. So a smart tactic might be to scour the area for monster hunters to point in the general direction of the werewolves, even if it means killing people and framing the werewolves for it. Also, werewolves often have human lives and identities. In the fiction throughout the core book, the werewolves had their lives upturned by a beshilu who inhabited a cop, then sending the rest of the police force after them. A vampire, providing one of them had a nicely placed ghoul or dominate, would be able to do something similar. With human forms wanted by the police, animal control alerted to rabid, wild dogs, the werewolves are likely to have a hard time to operate.<br /> <br /> There's ways around this, of course, the werewolves could just jump into the Hisil or start stealing skins. Alternatively if war were declared, the werewolves would just start a Siskur-Dah, then hunt the vampires down during the day and rip them to shreds. But, like I said, there's no reason for that to happen outside of special circumstances. If they were merciful, they might just stake them, ship them to Abu Dhabi in boxes and never look back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T13:21:48-08:00","id":801576,"title":"","content":"Replying to Shadow Knight. <br /> <br /> Let's just assume, that you as a vampire have dominate, and arrange for all of these things to happen. These overlaying threats. Number one, you have to do all of this without the Werewolves noticing. They are entrenched in their territory. Problem is, not only will and entrenched Pack with a dedicated locus be using Read the World's Loom, they will also be using Lore of the Land if at all possible. In addition, since they are set up to fight vampires, they will most likely have enacted wards against anything supernatural from a Kindred. Hey the Mekhet can learn about obscure spirit facets then the Werewolves certainly know about ghouls, and know when they are entering the territory now. With Lore of the Land<br /> <br /> &quot;Success: Each success reveals a single rite, spiritual resonance,<br /> or other supernatural, widespread effect affecting the<br /> territory that the Uratha is currently in. If used in the territory<br /> of the Uratha\u2019s pack, the Facet also reveals the presence of all<br /> creatures within Purity x 100 yards of his current position, as<br /> well as other threats such as fires, traps, pitfalls, or explosives.<br /> Only physically present creatures are detected, so Lore of the<br /> Land does not reveal spirits, ghosts, or other beings in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The Uratha may add his Purity to<br /> all rolls to navigate and move through the territory he is in<br /> for the remainder of the scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then of course you are neglecting spirit allies who will be watching for shit to go down and will inform the pack. Removing a pack from his territory is no easy thing.<br /> <br /> You need to play to a vampires strengths, trying to kill them via combat and traceable servants is not the way. Keeping your hands clean and turning all your resources to ruining their territory and exposing them to the mortal world is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:29:08-08:00","id":802430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=799569#post799569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about just numbers I think the situation is: (BP 5 for vamp. and equivalent for Werewolf...at greater BP the balance hangs for the vampire I suppose)<br /> <br /> (I took it from an old topic)<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Werewolf in Gauru attack pool:</b> 5 Str + 3 (Gauru) + 2 (Merits that increase Strength) + 10 (for Crimson Spasm - I made a roll with 18 dice and dobled the successes) + 5 (Gift of Strength) + 5 Brawl -1 (Relentless Assault to gain +1 damage) = 29 dice, with 8-again from Killer Instinct (1st dot Rahu Auspice Gift)<br /> <b>Werewolf in Gauru damage pool:</b> 2 (teeth) + 1 (relentless assualt) + 1 (living weapon) + 5 (slaughterer) = + 9 lethal<br /> <b>Werewolf Defense:</b> 9 (Dex/Wits + Athletics)<br /> <b>Werewolf Health:</b> 5 (size) + 5 (Stamina) + 4 (Gauru) + 1 (Favored Form) + 5 (Warrior's Hide - 2nd dot Rahu Auspice Gift) = 20<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire attack pool:</b> 5 Str + 5 (Frenzy) + 5 (Passive Vigor) + 6 (3 vitae) + 5 Brawl = 26<br /> <b>Vampire damage pool:</b> +0 agg (claws of the unholy) + 5 (Active Vigor) = + 5 agg OR +2agg (feeding the Crone) + 5 (Active Vigor) = 7 agg<br /> <b>Vampire defense:</b> 9 (Gauru prevents you from adding any skill to defense so just Dex/Wits + Celerity) but with Coil of the Wyrm 4 add 5 for BP and rise defense to 14<br /> <b>Vampire Health:</b> 5 (size) + 5 (Stamina) + 5 (Resilience) + 5 BP (Coil of the wyrm 4) = 20<br /> <br /> I've ignored the Efficient Killer merit because I think the drawback (&quot;This Merit only works on living targets with discernible weak points&quot;) rules out Vampires (if there's something to contradict this I'd love to know).&quot;<br /> <br /> So the pools are 2-3 dice lower (the 8 again can be compensated from 5 more defense) and this not sound to me as an impossible match for the vamp.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to say this REALLY undersells the Garou. First and Foremost, you ignored the All-out attack bonus for a Werewolf who has relentless assault, that is another +2 dice. The second thing is totem bonuses, but this isn't really a issue as the werewolf may have a non combat focused totem.<br /> <br /> To get to vigor 5 as a Gangrel, you would need to throw down 20 XP. Celerity 20 XP Resilience and Protean 18, assuming one of these starts at 3 dots. 1 for Unholy claws. Coil of the Wyrm 16. BP 25 in order to be at BP in order to make him more combat effective as it were. <br /> <br /> The above Werewolf we will say is a Blood talon Rahu. He starts with 2 purity, one glory. His starting gifts are Slaughterer and Primal Strength. To raise his glory and Purity to 5, the base for this build and how he unlocks most of the gifts we need to spend 21 XP. 15 on Merits for favored form and relentless assault Period. As far as supernatural talents goes, that means the vampire is over an astounding 39 XP. 49, if you drop the Primal Urge down by 2, as he does not need to be that high of a Primal Urge to be combat effective like the vampire in frenzy does. That gives us a lot of room to maneuver this Werewolf into an even more powerful position.<br /> <br /> So based off of your formula, I will leave the Werewolf at Primal Urge of 5, but leaves him with 39 XP to dole out. <br /> <br /> At Purity 5, This Werewolf has the following gifts:<br /> <br /> Full Moon: 5<br /> Primal Strength<br /> Slaughterer<br /> Hit and Run(5 XP)<br /> <br /> At Glory 5, the Werewolf has the following gifts:<br /> <br /> Berserkers Might: (Agg damage to your claws is reduced to your successes)<br /> Fearless Hunter<br /> Black Earth, Red Hunger<br /> Predators Unmatched Pursuit<br /> <br /> At Honor 5(15 XP), the Werewolf has the following gifts:<br /> Perfected Rage<br /> Crushing Blow<br /> Lay Low the Challenger<br /> Knotted Paths<br /> Deny Everything<br /> <br /> At Cunning 5 (15XP), The Werewolf has the following gifts<br /> Unchained<br /> Incite Fury<br /> Natures Lure<br /> Feet of Mist<br /> Primal Allure.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now you have a werewolf able to soak damage, dodge with Hit and Run(Similar to celerity but unlimited.) When he hits he activates crushing blow, slaughterer, and lay low the challenger. Your Kindred now sufers -5 defense, -2 to physical rolls versus the werewolf without the expenditure of willpower, and takes a significant more amount of weapon damage then you are doling out. And We will just throw your 5 successes from crimson Spasm onto lethal damage instead. The Dice pool is big enough to gaurantee a hit, a +5L to increase the existing dicepool to +14 makes it a wonderful little boost in damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:43:00-08:00","id":802443,"title":"","content":"Only 4 pages for this to boil down into a white-room scenario of mind-numbing number-crunching. Took longer than I expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T17:15:34-08:00","id":802468,"title":"","content":"At least Hitler wasn't mentioned yet. Wait. Dammit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T02:56:36-08:00","id":802950,"title":"","content":"I think that most people are over the white-room number crunching. In general, a combat-focused wolf will be stronger than a combat focused vampire in a featureless white room using 2e rules. Until we get into some very strange &quot;elder versus super-alpha&quot; theorycraft build scenarios, which most of us aren't interested in. <br /> <br /> Fortunately, real games don't shake out that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T03:48:56-08:00","id":802960,"title":"","content":"I agree with MCN and probably my intentions in building this hypothetical scenario have been misunderstood. It was just a scenario to better understand the mechanics (at least for me cause I'm not so expert about werewolf) and I found all your tips very useful.<br /> So just two conclusive questions about this wihite room challange:<br /> <br /> 1) until Blood Potency 5 the werewolf can be strongher than vampire. Ok. After Blood Potency 5?? Does change something? (obviously against a similar experienced werwolf). <br /> 2) With Primeval Miasma, should be possible, go into mist becoming virtually immune to damage (Except for fire sources), heal up himself, drinking from the open wound of the werewolf (dealt with aggravated damages so he can't heal these wounds at the start of the turn) to restore vitae lost in this way, and come back to the fight?? Could this be a good strategy or the werewolf can avoid it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T04:42:09-08:00","id":802974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=802960#post802960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with MCN and probably my intentions in building this hypothetical scenario have been misunderstood. It was just a scenario to better understand the mechanics (at least for me cause I'm not so expert about werewolf) and I found all your tips very useful.<br /> So just two conclusive questions about this wihite room challange:<br /> <br /> 1) until Blood Potency 5 the werewolf can be strongher than vampire. Ok. After Blood Potency 5?? Does change something? (obviously against a similar experienced werwolf).<br /> 2) With Primeval Miasma, should be possible, go into mist becoming virtually immune to damage (Except for fire sources), heal up himself, drinking from the open wound of the werewolf (dealt with aggravated damages so he can't heal these wounds at the start of the turn) to restore vitae lost in this way, and come back to the fight?? Could this be a good strategy or the werewolf can avoid it?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I don't think it changes much, in my opinion.<br /> 2) I can see Primeval Miasma working as an effective strategy if a Werewolf uses any of the Weather Gifts to alter the environment. Just blend in with the fog and/or rain, and hope that the pack doesn't have control over Fire via the Elemental Gift or a spirit ally (heck, even a totem) with fire-based powers. On the other hand, I have to wonder if a vampire's Primeval Miasma form might be vulnerable to the Elemental Facet over Air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T08:48:58-08:00","id":803126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=802960#post802960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) until Blood Potency 5 the werewolf can be strongher than vampire. Ok. After Blood Potency 5?? Does change something? (obviously against a similar experienced werwolf).<br /> 2) With Primeval Miasma, should be possible, go into mist becoming virtually immune to damage (Except for fire sources), heal up himself, drinking from the open wound of the werewolf (dealt with aggravated damages so he can't heal these wounds at the start of the turn) to restore vitae lost in this way, and come back to the fight?? Could this be a good strategy or the werewolf can avoid it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well a vampire adds his Blood Potency to his strength when in Frenzy, so that's the primary thing that increases as far as combat capability goes. At a certain point that becomes hard to match even for a werewolf. Not sure 6 or 7 is that point though. And I guess how much vitae you can use per turn to power Physical Intensity also increases, which <i>might</i> be enough to overwhelm a werewolf before his healing has a chance to kick in.<br /> <br /> Still a tall order for a vampire to beat a rahu, though.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Primeval Miasma is certainly a great tactic to avoid having to duke it out on the werewolf's terms, but as has already been mentioned, a variety of Weather Gifts could probably protect the werewolf. And Tongue of Flame (Elemental Gift Purity Facet) puts a quick end to that if we're throwing in extra abilities. Though why a werewolf with that gift would even have been fighting in the first place, I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 01-07-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T08:49:46-08:00","id":803127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=802443#post802443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only 4 pages for this to boil down into a white-room scenario of mind-numbing number-crunching. Took longer than I expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread has been plenty useful so far and if a couple of peolpe want to/enjoy a bit of nimber crunching alongside the rest of the discussion then I don't see any problem. Even if the characters being created and tested are not practical they do highlight to me what different abilities/powers I can look for in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T10:25:10-08:00","id":803193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803126#post803126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well a vampire adds his Blood Potency to his strength when in Frenzy, so that's the primary thing that increases as far as combat capability goes. At a certain point that becomes hard to match even for a werewolf. And I guess how much vitae you can use per turn to power Physical Intensity also increases, which might be enough to overwhelm a werewolf before his healing has a chance to kick in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is what I supposed about rising BP, cause it not just add in strenght while in frenzy, but allowing to spend one or two more vitae it means 2/4 more dice for BP 6-7. Furthemore it can add also in Defense and Health. Thank you for your consideration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803126#post803126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, Primeval Miasma is certainly a great tactic to avoid having to duke it out on the werewolf's terms, but as has already been mentioned, a variety of Weather Gifts could probably protect the werewolf. And Tongue of Flame (Elemental Gift Purity Facet) puts a quick end to that if we're throwing in extra abilities. Though why a werewolf with that gift would even have been fighting in the first place, I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I'm not too much expert about all the werewolf gifts. I have to study them better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T10:30:24-08:00","id":803199,"title":"","content":"Tongue of flame is probably the number one power in the Uratha's anti-vampire arsenal, but I suspect most werewolves don't actually know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T11:01:23-08:00","id":803218,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind though that werewolf healing rises dramatically at higher levels as well, and anything trying to influence them suffers twice their Primal Urge as a penalty. Plus, werewolves arguably have more varied uses for being able to spend more Essence per turn than a vampire does. Berserker's Might/Resilience, Hit &amp;Run/Celerity, Slaughterer/Vigor, 1 for Full Healing, but then after that you still have Crushing Blow, Unchained, Lay Low the Challenger, Tongue of Flame (or any elemental gift), Fog of War, One Step Ahead, Shield Breaker, All Doors Locked, Grasp of Howling Winds. All could be important in turning the tides of a fight. These things are too complicated to truly white room anyway, honestly.<br /> <br /> And then if the werewolf death rages he just gets have of those for free anyway and can probably just outlast the vampire till his vitae runs out or the sun rises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T11:49:16-08:00","id":803239,"title":"","content":"One thing that's always overlooked is teh &quot;Feed&quot; move. If a vamp gets a dramatic success in a grapple - not that hard with all the successes flying about from frenzy/blood boosting etc - he can choose both damage move and feed move. This adds an effective blood potency in successes damage to each successful grapple - and allows the vampire to recharge during combat - something not as easy for the wolf.<br /> <br /> It makes topping out in blood-boosting for a grapple really attractive; even at BP3, the vamp can add 6 dice (nine in frenzy) to any grapple pool; if any of that gives a dramatic success, the move become self-sustaining. Perhaps not enough to make sure the wolf is going down in death rage - but then again, if your ghouls/animalism summoned hoard/other minions are helping soften it up with bullets, it can help.<br /> <br /> Failing that, what is wrong with a silver bullet? Doesn't everyone know that's how to kill a werewolf? With celerity to keep out of range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:02:20-08:00","id":803247,"title":"","content":"Did anyone mention its probably a bad idea in general to bite a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:13:00-08:00","id":803254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803239#post803239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that's always overlooked is teh &quot;Feed&quot; move. If a vamp gets a dramatic success in a grapple - not that hard with all the successes flying about from frenzy/blood boosting etc - he can choose both damage move and feed move. This adds an effective blood potency in successes damage to each successful grapple - and allows the vampire to recharge during combat - something not as easy for the wolf.<br /> <br /> It makes topping out in blood-boosting for a grapple really attractive; even at BP3, the vamp can add 6 dice (nine in frenzy) to any grapple pool; if any of that gives a dramatic success, the move become self-sustaining. Perhaps not enough to make sure the wolf is going down in death rage - but then again, if your ghouls/animalism summoned hoard/other minions are helping soften it up with bullets, it can help.<br /> <br /> Failing that, what is wrong with a silver bullet? Doesn't everyone know that's how to kill a werewolf? With celerity to keep out of range?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that the problem for the Bite is that in the next turn the Werewolf will probably win the contested roll and gain the control fo the grapple. This is due to the 8's again gift. Quite the same pool but with 8 again...). Or am I missing anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:33:26-08:00","id":803271,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't know that a grapple is necessarily in the favor of the vampire, even with Physical Intensity. <br /> <br /> There are a lot of potential factors to consider. Unchained. Protean 4, Garou Strength, Primal Strength, Physical Intensity, Vigor, Favored Form Attribute Bonuses, Crimson Spasm, Killer Instinct, Frenzy Potency Bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:34:44-08:00","id":803272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803247#post803247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone mention its probably a bad idea in general to bite a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Werewolves do lethal damage to vampires on biting them and can immediately initiate a grapple if they choose to. Seems silly not to in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:36:29-08:00","id":803275,"title":"","content":"I think the implication was that a werewolf would get blood bonded, but I don't believe it would necessarily work that way, or if it did, that it would matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:40:30-08:00","id":803278,"title":"","content":"Ah, right. Yeah I don't think just tasting the blood does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:42:29-08:00","id":803279,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't bleed when cut. normally. It would take some presence of mind to direct vitae down a werewolf's throat while he's chewing your arm off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:47:44-08:00","id":803283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803275#post803275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the implication was that a werewolf would get blood bonded, but I don't believe it would necessarily work that way, or if it did, that it would matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is exactly the implication, your biting, your going to get blood in your mouth. Yes it does lethal damage, but it most certainly is going to be a problem with the blood. You have to be sure to get the kill right then such as with Efficient Killer (thats a lot of damage but not sure if that is exactly how that works as characters still get defense against others in that case, and the whole 'living targets' thing, since vampires while having discernible weak points don't match both criteria).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:50:21-08:00","id":803284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803279#post803279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't bleed when cut. normally. It would take some presence of mind to direct vitae down a werewolf's throat while he's chewing your arm off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No but they will have it in the area bitten, and vampires automatically take one on a bite. Its why they don't bite each other in combat much. I would figure this rule applies in crossover too, though was not necessary to include in werewolf where its really not an issue against most things they bite. There was a big discussion on this during the open development stage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:57:26-08:00","id":803291,"title":"","content":"I think one of the books describes Vitae as actually pulling away from a severed limb and back into the vampire's body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Blood</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, Vitae is so obedient that even when a vampire is injured in a fashion that would cause a mortal\u2019s blood to spurt forth, Vitae hesitates, seemingly defying the very laws of physics, unwilling to do anything without a direct order from the vampire to do so. What\u2019s more, for the few moments after Vitae exits a vampire\u2019s body \u2014 prior to reverting back to ordinary blood \u2014 the fluid remains under the authority of the vampire. A severed finger can literally be summoned back to the hand from which it came by the mere will of the injured party.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is first edition, though.<br /> <br /> The big thing that's going to tip the tables towards the werewolf, or really anyone except for other vampires, is the ability to move around during daylight unhindered. Presumably one of the big reason there is a vampire society, despite their territoriality and animosity and all those other sweet vices, is they are aware of how fast things can escalate when every vampire has a ghoul who knows the weaknesses of vampires and is willing to do anything for you. You have the traditions, you have allies, you have all manner of decorum keeping you and other vampires safe from other vampires and you.<br /> <br /> But once you start meddling in the affairs of others, particularly things that can tear a ghoul in half without breaking a sweat, or devolve a pack of ghouled dogs with Supernal magic, you're going to want to close ranks, be as stealthy as possible, and start saving Experiences to raise your Safe Haven and Persuasion so you can find a way to avoid being stabbed with a piece of wood while you're asleep.<br /> <br /> I know it's overlooked a lot, and it makes sense why, because how are you going to have a versus competition when one side is sleeping, but it's a bigger weak point than fire when you're talking about vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:59:18-08:00","id":803292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803199#post803199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tongue of flame is probably the number one power in the Uratha's anti-vampire arsenal, but I suspect most werewolves don't actually know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a must if you want to actually exterminate Hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:01:46-08:00","id":803297,"title":"","content":"Yeah I doubt there's much of a risk of blood bond from the bite.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if a gangrel could take the skin of a werewolf though to get the benefits of one of their forms. And if the supernatural features of those forms would remain in tact. Probably not, but it'd be fun to have Garou healing on my Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:02:39-08:00","id":803298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803291#post803291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the books describes Vitae as actually pulling away from a severed limb and back into the vampire's body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That is first edition, though.<br /> <br /> The big thing that's going to tip the tables towards the werewolf, or really anyone except for other vampires, is the ability to move around during daylight unhindered. Presumably one of the big reason there is a vampire society, despite their territoriality and animosity and all those other sweet vices, is they are aware of how fast things can escalate when every vampire has a ghoul who knows the weaknesses of vampires and is willing to do anything for you. You have the traditions, you have allies, you have all manner of decorum keeping you and other vampires safe from other vampires and you.<br /> <br /> But once you start meddling in the affairs of others, particularly things that can tear a ghoul in half without breaking a sweat, or devolve a pack of ghouled dogs with Supernal magic, you're going to want to close ranks, be as stealthy as possible, and start saving Experiences to raise your Safe Haven and Persuasion so you can find a way to avoid being stabbed with a piece of wood while you're asleep.<br /> <br /> I know it's overlooked a lot, and it makes sense why, because how are you going to have a versus competition when one side is sleeping, but it's a bigger weak point than fire when you're talking about vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the big sticker to be sure.<br /> <br /> (Pun Intended)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:04:18-08:00","id":803300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803297#post803297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I doubt there's much of a risk of blood bond from the bite.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if a gangrel could take the skin of a werewolf though to get the benefits of one of their forms. And if the supernatural features of those forms would remain in tact. Probably not, but it'd be fun to have Garou healing on my Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Skin? Why Skin? Beasts Skin doesn't require skinning or anything like that. What are you talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:05:15-08:00","id":803301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803239#post803239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Failing that, what is wrong with a silver bullet? Doesn't everyone know that's how to kill a werewolf? With celerity to keep out of range?</div> </div> </div> </div>A werewolf is probably faster than a vampire with Celerity if he has Unmatched Pursuit, and then he can also dodge bullets with his normal defense + Hit &amp; Run or Fog of War, so it's sort of just moot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:07:15-08:00","id":803303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803300#post803300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skin? Why Skin? Beasts Skin doesn't require skinning or anything like that. What are you talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was just using Skin Thief terms because of the common word. That's the one I'm talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:18:49-08:00","id":803313,"title":"","content":"I'm still of the opinion that a blood bond is at risk on bite, as vampires can reflexively spend vitae and maneuver it. Otherwise you wouldn't be able to feed vitae to humans in any way that is subtle or remove it. And a grapple with the teeth is sure to risk it. It would cost the vampire 1 vitae that could be used otherwise though I would think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V:tR2E pg. 94</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is to say, on a successful attack,<br /> they cause lethal damage equal to their successes, even to<br /> Kindred. As well, the attacker also takes one Vitae (which<br /> causes an additional point of lethal damage to mortals).</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, does Efficient Killer go into effect in grapples? Nobody is technically denied their defense. Has this question been asked in the Werewolf Forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:37:09-08:00","id":803322,"title":"","content":"That's because you're looking at a Kindred bite as opposed to a Werewolf bite. The Kindred bite there assumes that you <i>want </i>to take Vitae from your victim, because that's part of their M.O. That's not really a werewolf thing.<br /> <br /> A werewolf bite does not assume you're ingesting any of your victim's flesh or blood, and in fact there is a specific and clear distinction made between a werewolf who bites and a werewolf who bites with the intent to feed/ingest/swallow, as the latter (when used against other Uratha or Humans) grants the Werewolf Essence, does aggravated damage, and is a violation of the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as the Efficient Killer Grapple thing, I'd wager it'd work if you use the Hold Maneuver then I'd say it'd work when used from the outside (and from the inside if you got an exceptional success and do use Damage as your second maeuver.) I'd have to reread the merit though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:39:14-08:00","id":803325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803301#post803301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A werewolf is probably faster than a vampire with Celerity if he has Unmatched Pursuit, and then he can also dodge bullets with his normal defense + Hit &amp; Run or Fog of War, so it's sort of just moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>mmm I don't think Werewolf would be faster then a Vampire with celerity above 2. Unmatched Pursuit double the speed, celerity multiply the speed for celerity+1. Furthemore Blood Potency is added to the speed during frenzy, same for Vigor (passively). And if the werewolf uses the jump enhancement, it count as an action, so when he lands he couldn't attack and would be liable to a Vampire's attack. Hit and run and fog of war are contested rolls so it's not sure they have success and every turn they are in the same situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-07-2016, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:42:55-08:00","id":803329,"title":"","content":"Hit and Run is only contested for the Stealth portion. It automatically interrupts the action.<br /> <br /> You're right about Unmatched pursuit though. It does add Glory to speed, and then considering Urhan and Urshul speed I'd say that generally puts you at about equivalent to Celerity 2 with the doubling. But anything higher and you're not catching that vampire (except maybe with Chase Down). So fair point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:45:35-08:00","id":803331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803329#post803329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hit and Run is only contested for the Stealth portion. It automatically interrupts the action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you are right, but if the vampire uses his interrupt too, it become a clash of will, so contested. If the vampire can't use it, yes it's an automatic effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:45:56-08:00","id":803332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803313#post803313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still of the opinion that a blood bond is at risk on bite, as vampires can reflexively spend vitae and maneuver it. Otherwise you wouldn't be able to feed vitae to humans in any way that is subtle or remove it. And a grapple with the teeth is sure to risk it. It would cost the vampire 1 vitae that could be used otherwise though I would think.<br /> <br /> Also, does Efficient Killer go into effect in grapples? Nobody is technically denied their defense. Has this question been asked in the Werewolf Forum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, First stage of blood bond does not makes some Kindred immune to the Siskur Dah. Because that's what it'd be. The Uratha would be conflicted shortly after the decomposed thing off is dropped off it's Gauru muzzle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:47:57-08:00","id":803334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803331#post803331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes you are right, but if also the vampire uses his interrupt it become a clash of will, so contested. If the vampire can't use it, yes it's an automatic effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would making it a clash of wills help in preventing a bullet dodge? I'm not sure I understand how that would work. Does the Clash happen before the bullet is fired? Or is this some Wanted type nonsense? This is an actual question. I guess since the Clash Occurs before the roll it should in theory apply before it's fired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:47:58-08:00","id":803335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803329#post803329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hit and Run is only contested for the Stealth portion. It automatically interrupts the action.<br /> <br /> You're right about Unmatched pursuit though. It does add Glory to speed, and then considering Urhan and Urshul speed I'd say that generally puts you at about equivalent to Celerity 2 with the doubling. But anything higher and you're not catching that vampire (except maybe with Chase Down). So fair point.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forget, the Uratha isn't limited to using only 1 essence for Unmatched Pursuit. They could invest all they got for their turn on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:51:25-08:00","id":803337,"title":"","content":"Also what happens if you Hit and Run, then Chase Down, two Clashes of WIll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:18:52-08:00","id":803352,"title":"","content":"Would Kindred Dueling 4 (Pincushion) be effective against werewolves healing? I could certainly see it working due to how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:43:17-08:00","id":803366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803352#post803352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Kindred Dueling 4 (Pincushion) be effective against werewolves healing? I could certainly see it working due to how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think yes because the mechanics is the same, but it's not so efficient against werewolf cause I suppose you can take with you just one big weapon, so you can let it inside the Garou just one time. Not sufficient to take him down. Better with Aggravate damage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:46:08-08:00","id":803370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803337#post803337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also what happens if you Hit and Run, then Chase Down, two Clashes of WIll?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think yes. Clash of Will take place everytime two effects enter in conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:48:23-08:00","id":803373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803335#post803335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You forget, the Uratha isn't limited to using only 1 essence for Unmatched Pursuit. They could invest all they got for their turn on it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you mean? Unmatched Pursuit is an istant action at essence 1 cost. I don't think you can use it more time in the same turn. Probably I didn't understand what you mean cause my bad english :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T15:56:37-08:00","id":803399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803373#post803373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What do you mean? Unmatched Pursuit is an istant action at essence 1 cost. I don't think you can use it more time in the same turn. Probably I didn't understand what you mean cause my bad english :P</div> </div> </div> </div>The gift reads: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">and may reflexively spend 1 Essence to double her Speed in any form for one turn.&quot; </span></span><br /> <br /> Spend 6 points (Doable with Dedicated Locus)? and you tell me what's say, 15*2*2*2*2*2 = 900 speed, in one turn. That's half a mile. In 3 seconds.<br /> <br /> That's 6000 miles per hour.<br /> <br /> That's Mach 7,8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-07-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T16:08:46-08:00","id":803407,"title":"","content":"I always read that as pay 1 Essence, double your Speed. Period. You can do it. Once. Not pay Essence till your limit and break the sound barrier seven times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T16:22:56-08:00","id":803410,"title":"","content":"That's a fetish right there if ever I saw one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T16:54:41-08:00","id":803421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803399#post803399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The gift reads: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">and may reflexively spend 1 Essence to double her Speed in any form for one turn.&quot; </span></span><br /> <br /> Spend 6 points (Doable with Dedicated Locus)? and you tell me what's say, 15*2*2*2*2*2 = 900 speed, in one turn. That's half a mile. In 3 seconds.<br /> <br /> That's 6000 miles per hour.<br /> <br /> That's Mach 7,8.</div> </div> </div> </div>O.o Well it sounds broken to me... Werewolf are Gods XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T16:59:53-08:00","id":803424,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing about Reflexive actions. You get as many as the ST says you do. Many times, the assumption is that you'll get to do these things once. In 1e, there was parkour that let you reflexively make a jump forwards. Some people tried to twist that into infinite leaps moving forward, so you could, in theory, move as far as you wanted without ever using your turn. <br /> <br /> Don't be that person. Use reflexive actions responcibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:05:45-08:00","id":803426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803407#post803407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always read that as pay 1 Essence, double your Speed. Period. You can do it. Once. Not pay Essence till your limit and break the sound barrier seven times.</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes a first point of essence and an instant action to activate, then you can literally burn all your essence to give the Flash a run for his money. Read the description below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:10:25-08:00","id":803429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803424#post803424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing about Reflexive actions. You get as many as the ST says you do. Many times, the assumption is that you'll get to do these things once. In 1e, there was parkour that let you reflexively make a jump forwards. Some people tried to twist that into infinite leaps moving forward, so you could, in theory, move as far as you wanted without ever using your turn.<br /> <br /> Don't be that person. Use reflexive actions responcibly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The specific example you're quoting, made athletics reflexive, meaning the person didn't needed to roll it, at all. And could carry on other actions while moving like a veritable ninja. Also, it's typed &quot;responsibly&quot;.<br /> <br /> Breathing is reflexive, walking is reflexive. Shit that doesn't requires you to roll is reflexive. I don't see any reason why, if a PC can spend 10 essence a turn, not to let them burn their whole pool for a quite Glorious display of spiritual potency. Beyond &quot;Wah, my Celerity 5 vampire can't keep up!&quot;<br /> <br /> In this case? The user gets as many reflexive actions as essence he can spend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:37:06-08:00","id":803443,"title":"","content":"Counterpoint: I once asked if a werewolf in death rage would get the doubled speed for free, and the dev answered in the affirmative. If you could spend as much as you liked on the power, that would be literally infinite speed, which I suspect they would have mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:40:57-08:00","id":803446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803429#post803429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The specific example you're quoting, made athletics reflexive, meaning the person didn't needed to roll it, at all. And could carry on other actions while moving like a veritable ninja. Also, it's typed &amp;quot;responsibly&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Breathing is reflexive, walking is reflexive. Shit that doesn't requires you to roll is reflexive. I don't see any reason why, if a PC can spend 10 essence a turn, not to let them burn their whole pool for a quite Glorious display of spiritual potency. Beyond &amp;quot;Wah, my Celerity 5 vampire can't keep up!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> In this case? The user gets as many reflexive actions as essence he can spend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like you said: probably the meaning of the reflexive in this case, as for to breath and walk, is that you can use the essence for this effect without limiting other actions that require essence, not that you can spend it more than once per turn. <br /> <br /> Anyway I don't know the real intention of the developers so ST, as usually, can interprets it as he want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:49:43-08:00","id":803452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803443#post803443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counterpoint: I once asked if a werewolf in death rage would get the doubled speed for free, and the dev answered in the affirmative. If you could spend as much as you liked on the power, that would be literally infinite speed, which I suspect they would have mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it gets activated for free. Read, the essence you have to burn + the instant action.<br /> <br /> It reads so. It takes no cost to -activate- it. Not to use the other essence use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:58:35-08:00","id":803457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803407#post803407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always read that as pay 1 Essence, double your Speed. Period. You can do it. Once. Not pay Essence till your limit and break the sound barrier seven times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. I think this is one of those cases where you have two seemingly valid ways to read something, but one reading gives you seemingly wonky and out of scale results. It's almost always best/correct to go with the more conservative/less ridiculous interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:14:51-08:00","id":803469,"title":"","content":"Eh, if a player of mine wants to burn all his essence to GET THE FUCK OUT OF DODGE<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2122 (whilst likely leaving his packmates in the dust of the conflict) I'll let him.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:25:05-08:00","id":803474,"title":"","content":"I think celerity still ends up outdoing unmatched pursuit in the long run. Celerity 5 spend 1 BP get x6 speed for the turn, and it adds to your defense. To be moving just as fast, the Werewolf needs to spending about twice the essence. Sure he can move faster at n expedited cost, but burning essence quickly won't end well.<br /> <br /> Tortoise and the hare. Werewolf might be faster if the rules allow more than one essence to be spent on predators unmatched pursuit, but a vampire with celerity will interrupt and catch you before you even leave, and barring that, chase you down, maybe a little slower, but with vitae in store when he catches up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:44:12-08:00","id":803486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803469#post803469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, if a player of mine wants to burn all his essence to GET THE FUCK OUT OF DODGE<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2122 (whilst likely leaving his packmates in the dust of the conflict) I'll let him.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest way (imo) to decide is to honestly answer the question, do you <i>really</i> think the writers and developers intended the power to allow mach 7 werewolves? If the answer is no then chances are it's either being interpreted wrong, or was written incorrectly and wasn't caught during development and is in need of errata. For me, I can't quite imagine that this was the writers intentions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T19:08:35-08:00","id":803497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=802443#post802443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only 4 pages for this to boil down into a white-room scenario of mind-numbing number-crunching. Took longer than I expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had a good laugh at this. I haven't gotten into 2e yet, mostly because I'm still big on Mummy at the moment. But if I do so and in the interest of not reliving all the annoying stuff from World of Darkness days with Garou and Kindred. I'd be looking to have the rules be more than, &quot;Run from big scary werewolf.&quot; Since threads like these tend to be rather monofocused, I'm assuming, as one poster put it, that it rarely plays out any particular way with typical PC's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T20:45:54-08:00","id":803549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803486#post803486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest way (imo) to decide is to honestly answer the question, do you <i>really</i> think the writers and developers intended the power to allow mach 7 werewolves? If the answer is no then chances are it's either being interpreted wrong, or was written incorrectly and wasn't caught during development and is in need of errata. For me, I can't quite imagine that this was the writers intentions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me? I sincerely think that if I'm burning a net total of 7 essence to play Flash an homage is a fair trade. For 5 you can revive the Chicago fire with another gift.<br /> <br /> And it's not even the most absurd things you'll see in anyone's table. *grumbles about demons making it rain body-parts with a cloud of concrete eating bacteria that could decimate a city by just shedding a mere rank 2 cover.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-07-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T20:51:53-08:00","id":803552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803549#post803549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Me? I sincerely think that if I'm burning a net total of 7 essence to play Flash an homage is a fair trade. For 5 you can revive the Chicago fire with another gift.<br /> <br /> And it's not even the most absurd things you'll see in anyone's table. *grumbles about demons making it rain body-parts with a cloud of concrete eating bacteria that could decimate a city by just shedding a mere rank 2 cover.*</div> </div> </div> </div>Then at this point I guess we'll just have to agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T04:33:51-08:00","id":803657,"title":"","content":"About the mach 7 thing, this guy here says hi:<br /> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/p__/images/d/de/Sonic_the_Werehog.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20150109020719&amp;path-prefix=protagonist\" target=\"_blank\">http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/...ix=protagonist</a><br /> <br /> On topic: \u200b<br /> Can a vampire with coil of the voivode submit a werewolf to a full vinculum if the werewolf bite him?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:01:24-08:00","id":803665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803657#post803657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> On topic: \u200b<br /> Can a vampire with coil of the voivode submit a werewolf to a full vinculum if the werewolf bite him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I think yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:09:12-08:00","id":803669,"title":"","content":"If so, this means that during the fight, after a werewolf has been blood bonded from eating a portion of the vampire, the vampire gains a bonus to Social and Discipline rolls against the werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:23:36-08:00","id":803677,"title":"","content":"After a little thinking, this scene formed in my head:<br /> <br /> &quot;As the Wolf torn the vampire flesh, devouring his dead arm, the Dragon commanded his blood to do his bidding, bounding the giant beast to the Dragon will, with the voice of the thunder he shouted:<br /> - STOP!<br /> <br /> the Wolf stopped. And to this day, the Wolf guards the Dragon's Nest.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 01-08-2016, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:33:39-08:00","id":803679,"title":"","content":"While it's possible that might work, if a werewolf is in death rage mind control in that manner is going to be very difficult.<br /> <br /> And a werewolf who isn't able to hunt is going to be a very weak one indeed, without Essence and unable to change after a while. They don't do well in captivity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-08-2016, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:51:23-08:00","id":803683,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure blood bonds aren't strong enough to stop someone who's actively trying to murder you any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:12:56-08:00","id":803689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803683#post803683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure blood bonds aren't strong enough to stop someone who's actively trying to murder you any more.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes they are. I don't know about some creatures(Changelings, Werewolfs, etc), but anything with humanity/integrity will have a hard time trying to attack a regnant.<br /> <br /> About the scene I wrote, I did not specify the vampire clan or werewolf tribe, I was thinking about a Dragon Ventrue against a Ghost Wolf.\u200b This scene almost happened in one of my games, in the real outcome, the Wolf died from a silver bullet shot on his head(not from the vampire, another person made the shot).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T06:24:38-08:00","id":803693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803689#post803689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they are. I don't know about some creatures(Changelings, Werewolfs, etc), but anything with humanity/integrity will have a hard time trying to attack a regnant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you can guess where this is going.<br /> <br /> My character's first encounter with a vampire went something like this.<br /> <br /> 'Who's that?'<br /> 'Why do they smell like death?'<br /> 'Where'd they go? They turned invisible, I better be - ouch.'<br /> A look down revealed a syringe in his chest.<br /> 'I don't feel so h-'<br /> Then he woke up a little bit later in a bathroom with ghouls rifling through his clothing and trying to see if he had any Pure marks on him.<br /> <br /> Second encounter ended with sex, so it wasn't all bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:13:20-08:00","id":803750,"title":"","content":"You can't blood bond a werewolf biting you. There is a huge difference between a werewolf biting, and digesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:37:17-08:00","id":803762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803750#post803750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't blood bond a werewolf biting you. There is a huge difference between a werewolf biting, and digesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>While probably true, I don't imagine many werewolves know <i>not</i> to swallow the blow that's flowing into their gullet. They're used to eating all sorts of crazy things (spirit flesh made manifest, for instance). Unless they know about how the Vinculum works, I wouldn't give my players the opportunity to say &quot;I don't swallow.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:46:14-08:00","id":803772,"title":"","content":"Well...a little bit of blood would go down anyway. <br /> If you have in your mouth cyanide, you'd be poisoned even if you don't swallow. A litle bit is absorbed anyway.<br /> Another ST decision I think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T09:40:55-08:00","id":803808,"title":"","content":"What I'm getting from the continued discussion is that the Vampires only have a chance if they have a huge information advantage and hold the initiative, escalating way faster than the Werewolves and making them dead/gone before the wolves realise what's happening. Once the Werewolves know the fight is on they can identify and counter most social, political, etc. attacks through their Gifts and declare a hunt and win during the day.<br /> <br /> Step 1 for the Vampires is probably leaving their feeding grounds and moving around frequently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T09:51:19-08:00","id":803813,"title":"","content":"IIRC the bond didn't happened out of 3 immediate sips, they had to be across different nights. And a first stage bind isn't strong enough to stop an Uratha who's called the Siskur-Dah on you and is in Gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T09:58:17-08:00","id":803817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803813#post803813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC the bond didn't happened out of 3 immediate sips, they had to be across different nights. And a first stage bind isn't strong enough to stop an Uratha who's called the Siskur-Dah on you and is in Gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doesn't exactly say it has to be 3 nights, though that is the way it has been interpreted mostly. However, Coil of the Voivode only needs 1 sip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:02:11-08:00","id":803819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803813#post803813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC the bond didn't happened out of 3 immediate sips, they had to be across different nights. And a first stage bind isn't strong enough to stop an Uratha who's called the Siskur-Dah on you and is in Gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With Coil of the Voivode (Call to Serve) one drink is enough:<br /> &quot;...When building a blood bond (p. 99) the Dragon may bleed additional Vitae to<br /> expedite the process. Three Vitae will take her subject straight into<br /> a stage-two blood bond, while five pushes him all the way to stage<br /> three with a single sip. This Vitae must be shared over no more than<br /> a few minutes, but is not subject to limits on Vitae per turn.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Vitae is not linked to the quantity of the blood. Using Vitae, in fact, doesn't let the vampire without blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-08-2016, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:17:41-08:00","id":803823,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure a werewolf wouldn't be hesitant to swallow anything that leaks out of the bit of walking corpse he just tore off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:22:48-08:00","id":803826,"title":"","content":"That's a fair point as well, a bite isn't a swallow. And devouring flesh is something werewolves do only on certain occasions, while biting is something they do often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:27:10-08:00","id":803828,"title":"","content":"Well, when vampires bite they have no choice whether to ingest or not and they have less impressive fangs than werewolves in most of their forms. Vampires taking a point of Vitae during a bite is not written as an option, but a fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:42:45-08:00","id":803842,"title":"","content":"Werewolves aren't walking blood vacuums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:47:14-08:00","id":803844,"title":"","content":"Hah! Walking blood vaccums. My character is using that on reference to Kindred next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:38:49-08:00","id":803939,"title":"","content":"If you go strictly by the book, werewolves can't be blood bonded, anyway. Only mortals and vampires are subject to Vinculum. Other supernatural creatures can become addicted to Vitae, but getting a raging lupine monster addicted to the blood in your veins is a sure way to lose said blood in a hurry. The point is moot, but even so establishing Vinculum probably doesn't matter for the throes of frenzied battle, and once the vampire is dead ceases to matter entirely.<br /> <br /> Werewolves do not automatically ingest flesh and blood as they bite. This is explicitly laid out in the book on page 100. A werewolf is certainly going to taste the blood on her tongue, at least if she's biting a living creature. Vampires are a different and much stranger case, since they explicitly don't bleed like mortals do. I personally would say the biting werewolf is still going to get <i>some </i>blood and taste its sweetness, but not enough to track by (as is implied by the section under Wolf Senses on page 94). Not enough to count as a drink, either, for purposes of blood addiction, so the vampire would have to force the issue. Those thinking that pushing Vitae down the werewolf's throat will win them the fight will quickly meet disappointment (and Final Death shortly thereafter) when they realize those points are wasted or, at worst, have only made the werewolf more furious in her attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T13:00:43-08:00","id":803957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803939#post803939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go strictly by the book, werewolves can't be blood bonded, anyway. Only mortals and vampires are subject to Vinculum. Other supernatural creatures can become addicted to Vitae, but getting a raging lupine monster addicted to the blood in your veins is a sure way to lose said blood in a hurry. The point is moot, but even so establishing Vinculum probably doesn't matter for the throes of frenzied battle, and once the vampire is dead ceases to matter entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless Rose changed her mind, you would be wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire: The Requiem Rules FAQ (public)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can werewolves, mages, demons, and other monsters be blood bonded?<br /> <br /> Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T13:02:58-08:00","id":803960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803939#post803939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you go strictly by the book, werewolves can't be blood bonded, anyway. Only mortals and vampires are subject to Vinculum.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's no longer the case in Vampire 2e.<br /> <br /> Per Rose's FAQ:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Can werewolves, mages, demons, and other monsters be blood bonded?</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yes.</span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.g4exyxp463t2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.g4exyxp463t2\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.g4exyxp463t2\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.g4exyxp463t2 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T13:25:48-08:00","id":803972,"title":"","content":"Hm. Interesting. I never checked that part of the FAQ and the book itself doesn't say that. I prefer the first edition stance on it. Regardless, my other points stand: the blood bond isn't going to immediately help you against the werewolf in a fight, anyway. It does give a bonus to Discipline rolls, but I'd probably rather just spend the points on physical intensity to try to survive a bit longer in order to use any Disciplines on the werewolf. Breaking points are a bummer and all, but trying to force a Vinculum while also holding off a snarling <i>Gauru</i>-form werewolf is going to get you killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:09:38-08:00","id":803988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803683#post803683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure blood bonds aren't strong enough to stop someone who's actively trying to murder you any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly not a guaranteed success. WtF2 Death Rage - 'any attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha's course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer twice the werewolf's Primal Urge as a penalty. This is over and above any Supernatural Tolerance (p. 160) applied to supernatural powers'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:10:13-08:00","id":803989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803808#post803808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm getting from the continued discussion is that the Vampires only have a chance if they have a huge information advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... isn't that the modus operandi of most vampires? After all... &quot;<i>you're only immortal if you're smart.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> But I'll try to do a little more brainstorming. Sure werewolfs are absolute monster on hand-on-hand combat, but as someone already said earlier, a single Daeva could end the conflict before it even begins. In the end, it will boil down to the better strategy from the PC's. If 2 PC groups are entering in confront, there are too many things to consider. Like:<br /> <br /> - Which group have better resources, retainers, allies, contacts, safe place?<br /> Because you can simply use your social merits to shut down the social merits from another player.<br /> <br /> - Which group knows more about the other one?<br /> Well, silver bullets cost more than torches. And I'm just using common folklore on this one.<br /> <br /> - Who can spy the enemy better?<br /> Obfuscate and Auspex are easy to use, I read some things about werewolfs but nothing so easy as a single auto-hiding with on/off button or ask-a-question-about-something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:20:45-08:00","id":803997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803657#post803657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On topic: \u200b<br /> Can a vampire with coil of the voivode submit a werewolf to a full vinculum if the werewolf bite him?</div> </div> </div> </div> Absolutely. Though, its notable that the vinculum's main effect is to gather a Perfect Impression, which is going to have some rather strong role play considerations. Its not insta-you-do-what-I-say. Its abnsolutely <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803808#post803808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm getting from the continued discussion is that the Vampires only have a chance if they have a huge information advantage and hold the initiative,</div> </div> </div> </div> Not quite. They only have a chance if they avoid playing into the Werewolf hunting game, and play to their own strengths. Flat out, maintaining territories and hunting are two of the best strengths of the werewolf. When you play to werewolf strengths, the wolves win. If you play to vampire strengths, the vamps win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803939#post803939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves do not automatically ingest flesh and blood as they bite. This is explicitly laid out in the book on page 100.</div> </div> </div> </div> I assume you mean the line that goes, &quot;For every point of damage caused by an Uratha\u2019s bite, they can choose to ingest the flesh and gain a point of Essence.&quot; That's not exactly explicit, considering that is only talking about eating large chunks of flesh for essence, not mystical blood with addictive, drug-like properties you experience in the midst of an emotinoally charged, high adrenaline fight. Werewolves eat meat. They do not get essence from blood, so swallowing it is completely outside the scope of that paragraph.<br /> <br /> I'd argue for at least addiction for just tasting it at the absolute minimum. Which is still going to have interesting effects on combat. I think the rest is up to ST discretion - like so much with crossover, it comes down to what the ST wants for their games. So, I don't think you can say, with absolute authority, this is not a valid tactic that won't work no matter what. There are no rules, so each individual ST is going to have to make a call on the issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I personally would say the biting werewolf is still going to get <i>some </i>blood and taste its sweetness, but not enough to track by (as is implied by the section under Wolf Senses on page 94). </div> </div> </div> Vampires cannot be tracked through Taste of Blood, no matter how much is tasted or drank; only living targets can be tracked that way. Vampire blood is the accumlation of multiple mixed people's blood. Same thing in 1e. This does not imply anything about bite-and-drink-blood issues; this and that are separate, unrelated issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:29:39-08:00","id":804003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803989#post803989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Who can spy the enemy better?<br /> Obfuscate and Auspex are easy to use, I read some things about werewolfs but nothing so easy as a single auto-hiding with on/off button or ask-a-question-about-something.</div> </div> </div> </div>To put the Uratha side of information gathering in perspective:<br /> <br /> 1) Every werewolf can potentially:<br /> <br /> a) Notice someone distinctly lacks a pulse simply by applying their Wolf Senses hearing.<br /> <br /> b) Track not your scent or lack of thereof, but the disturbance in the photons that your shadow produced whilst you moved.<br /> <br /> c) Sick a spirit to shadow you and inform on your every move for days with Chorus. Good luck spotting it over the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> 2) Some werewolves can:<br /> <br /> a) Get an omen by gift or auspice given blessing that you're about to fuck with them.<br /> <br /> b) Simply command fire to do their bidding in violent supernatural eruptions that would teach Elders the definition of R\u00f6tschreck.<br /> <br /> c) Make you spiritually accept the role of prey, so that you act exactly the way they want you to better hunt you down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:31:13-08:00","id":804005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803989#post803989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Which group have better resources, retainers, allies, contacts, safe place?<br /> Because you can simply use your social merits to shut down the social merits from another player.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of werewolf facets that do this, and a couple merits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- Which group knows more about the other one?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, silver bullets cost more than torches. And I'm just using common folklore on this one.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also they can be dodged.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Who can spy the enemy better?<br /> Obfuscate and Auspex are easy to use, I read some things about werewolfs but nothing so easy as a single auto-hiding with on/off button or ask-a-question-about-something. </div> </div> </div>Hishu lets you hide in crowds, with a penalty to find you based on your Primal Urge. Scent Beneath the Surface acts as a lie detector, Know Thy Prey tells you your targets names, Allies, Contacts, Retainers, Resources, Staff and Status merits, Prey on Weakness tells you their Mask and Dirge, Scent of the Unnatural and a few other abilities detect vampires and ghouls, Bone Gnaw drags secrets from the bones you eat and isn't limited to old ones.<br /> <br /> At this point though we've wildly derailed from the original point of the thread and are moving, repeatedly, back into White Room 'who would win' situations that have nothing to do with the point.<br /> <br /> If people want to continue the discussion, can you make your own thread about the fight, while this one could continue dealing with 'how vampires could deal with warring over their territory with werewolves?' Keeping in mind, of course, that fighting them has already popped up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:55:44-08:00","id":804028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803997#post803997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves eat meat. They do not get essence from blood, so swallowing it is completely outside the scope of that paragraph.</div> </div> </div> </div>They eat flesh and blood of living things. Werewolves bite all kinds of enemies and aren't stated to explicitly swallow every time. Assuming they do, especially in a worst-case scenario, is just that, an assumption. Vampires are explicitly stated to not bleed in the same way as living creatures, so if we're making assumptions or interpreting the rules, &quot;werewolf biting vampire does not automatically mean werewolf drinks vampire's blood unless the vampire goes out of her way to force it&quot; is certainly valid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803997#post803997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue for at least addiction for just tasting it at the absolute minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is predicated upon the assumption that tasting equals drinking, and so every bite is also a drink. It's not. You have to actively drink Vitae. The closest I'd go is say that the taste of any blood on the tongue while biting is tantalizingly sweet, and from there it's up to the players and unfolding narrative whether the temptation is enough to entice more. But it's by no means guaranteed that you even taste Vitae while biting a vampire (as a werewolf), and then requires a roll to become addicted, anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T15:17:36-08:00","id":804048,"title":"","content":"At least in 1e, vitae tastes like blood, nothing sweet or appealing to it. Which makes addiction to it even more fucked up. If you're a ghoul at least you get something from that shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T15:58:07-08:00","id":804077,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in 2e it tastes a bit different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T16:46:09-08:00","id":804105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804077#post804077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, in 2e it tastes a bit different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T17:41:38-08:00","id":804146,"title":"","content":"Like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blood bearing Vitae is slightly darker, and has an almost<br /> syrupy quality. It has all the normal metallic smells blood<br /> should, but also has a subtle, sweet smell, like a dessert wine. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T17:43:38-08:00","id":804147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804105#post804105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like what?</div> </div> </div> </div> VtR 2nd pg 99<br /> &quot;Vitae is life. Life taste very, very good.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T18:31:18-08:00","id":804165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804028#post804028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They eat flesh and blood of living things.</div> </div> </div> </div> The section you referenced, about swallowing flesh for essence, specifically only says &quot;flesh.&quot; There is no reference to blood in there; in fact, there's nothing about that section that suggests werewolves can get essence from blood, which means that its all debatable. <u><i>You are extrapolating and making assumptions.</i></u> This is not a good thing, because that means you are making ST calls, which is just shy of a house rule. You are taking something, then pushing it further towards what you feel is appropriate for your view of werewolves. <br /> <br /> The problem with that is that, while what you are saying is fine for your specific games, it is not the same for all tables. I'm sorry, but other people are allowed to have different views on how all this interacts, and they're all as equally correct as you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T18:57:04-08:00","id":804196,"title":"","content":"Well, I think there's nothing much to say here. We already have 10 pages of what to do to kill a group of werewolfs trying to force a group of vampires off their territory(and vice-versa). I saw a bunch of numbers, a bunch of disciplines and a bunch of gifts and a good discussion about innate abilities. In the end I concluded that:<br /> &quot;If you ST wants to kill you, he can. You can be a member of a pack of werewolfs, if the ST wants, the vampires can surprise you, on the worse way possible, they can use Majesty or Dominate when you're on human form, or surprise you with Obfuscate, etc.<br /> You can be a member of a vampire coterie, if the ST wants, a pack of werewolfs can summon fire spirits to kill you, or they can hunt you during the day, or call siskur-dah on you and you're pretty much dead(again).\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm going to just observe and read this post from now on. I don't think that there's many more things to really add to the original purpose of the post.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 01-08-2016, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T19:04:26-08:00","id":804206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804165#post804165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The section you referenced, about swallowing flesh for essence, specifically only says &quot;flesh.&quot; There is no reference to blood in there; in fact, there's nothing about that section that suggests werewolves can get essence from blood, which means that its all debatable. <u><i>You are extrapolating and making assumptions.</i></u> This is not a good thing, because that means you are making ST calls, which is just shy of a house rule. You are taking something, then pushing it further towards what you feel is appropriate for your view of werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I very much am not. They can eat the flesh of living humans and wolves. This requires consuming their blood, too. They don't commit this sin by cooking human steaks, nor can they magically eat the flesh without also gulping down mouthfuls of blood. It's the way biology and predation meet through the vector of lupine jaws. I didn't mean to imply they get Essence from blood, but this isn't ambiguous. The very act of cannibalizing humans and wolves for Essence demands that they consume blood in large quantities as well.<br /> <br /> Werewolves don't consume blood and flesh without directly meaning to, except for minute amounts of blood that they probably swallow while biting\u2014not enough to matter for Vitae purposes. Vampires explicitly don't bleed like living creatures, and even with the blush of life active they bleed, but don't lose Vitae like it's blood. This is clearly stated in the book. Drinking Kindred Vitae is also a distinct act. It doesn't happen by accident, even if a werewolf bites a vampire. The vampire might force the issue by attempting to pour her Vitae down the werewolf's throat, such as in a grapple, but this requires an insane amount of risk for almost zero unlife-saving payoff. Vinculum isn't going to stop the werewolf from killing the vampire, and aside from a very specific power isn't going to be established fast enough to make a difference. The werewolf is tearing your face off <i>now</i>. Maybe she'll feel a Vitae-influenced guilt later, but that doesn't matter. The vampire's dead, the blood bond means nothing, and life goes on. Except for the vampire, of course.<br /> <br /> Does that clear up my stance on this matter? My earlier post inadvertently suggested that I meant you could gain Essence from blood alone; clarity is my burden (more so since I'm working on Changeling), so here I have attempted to clarify my thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":".  Too combative. 01-08-2016, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T19:40:06-08:00","id":804218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804206#post804206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I very much am not. They can eat the flesh of living humans and wolves. This requires consuming their blood, too. They don't commit this sin by cooking human steaks, nor can they magically eat the flesh without also gulping down mouthfuls of blood. It's the way biology and predation meet through the vector of lupine jaws. I didn't mean to imply they get Essence from blood, but this isn't ambiguous. The very act of cannibalizing humans and wolves for Essence demands that they consume blood in large quantities as well.<br /> <br /> Werewolves don't consume blood and flesh without directly meaning to, except for minute amounts of blood that they probably swallow while biting\u2014not enough to matter for Vitae purposes. Vampires explicitly don't bleed like living creatures, and even with the blush of life active they bleed, but don't lose Vitae like it's blood. This is clearly stated in the book. Drinking Kindred Vitae is also a distinct act. It doesn't happen by accident, even if a werewolf bites a vampire. The vampire might force the issue by attempting to pour her Vitae down the werewolf's throat, such as in a grapple, but this requires an insane amount of risk for almost zero unlife-saving payoff. Vinculum isn't going to stop the werewolf from killing the vampire, and aside from a very specific power isn't going to be established fast enough to make a difference. The werewolf is tearing your face off <i>now</i>. Maybe she'll feel a Vitae-influenced guilt later, but that doesn't matter. The vampire's dead, the blood bond means nothing, and life goes on. Except for the vampire, of course.<br /> <br /> Does that clear up my stance on this matter? My earlier post inadvertently suggested that I meant you could gain Essence from blood alone; clarity is my burden (more so since I'm working on Changeling), so here I have attempted to clarify my thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So what your saying then is vampires can't extract vitae at all, because obviously if they don't bleed they can't give vitae? So dripping blood and such doesn't work? Spiking a drink with vitae within seconds of it being sipped? A few drops on the tongue?<br /> <br /> Volume of blood is independent of vitae. A vampire could easily go into the fight intending to bleed if bitten. They control their vitae. Ever been attacked by a dog? Blood is immediate and in volume. Minor puncture wounds from nips are not indicative of an actual bite with an intent to harm. You don't have to tear chunks to produce large amounts of blood quickly. Any intelligent vampire would go into a fight with an enemy that will be biting with the intention to ensure they bleed if bitten unless their vitae reserves are very much limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T20:14:20-08:00","id":804228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804147#post804147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> VtR 2nd pg 99<br /> &quot;Vitae is life. Life taste very, very good.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>For vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T22:21:04-08:00","id":804259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804218#post804218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what your saying then is vampires can't extract vitae at all, because obviously if they don't bleed they can't give vitae? So dripping blood and such doesn't work? Spiking a drink with vitae within seconds of it being sipped? A few drops on the tongue?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that extracting Vitae by will or by force is a <i>conscious act</i>. It doesn't happen just by biting a vampire, at least for werewolves. They don't actively choose to gulp down flesh and blood with every bite. Vampires don't bleed Vitae and don't automatically force their Vitae down the gullet of everything that bites them. When a vampire bites someone, whether the initial bite attack or using the Feed move, they do drain Vitae, because it's what they do. In fact, the book actually says that <i>mortals </i>take one lethal damage per Vitae taken with the Feed move, or from the 1 Vitae taken automatically (which one assumes is voluntary) when they bite someone. The same section calls out werewolves as being immune to the effects of the bite where the word &quot;mortal&quot; is used, so you could even argue that they don't take lethal damage from being drained of Vitae.<br /> <br /> Either way, the stuff you're talking about is all a conscious decision, or the result of same, like forcing someone to drink. It doesn't happen automatically on a bite. Werewolves don't automatically ingest Vitae, even if the vampire would want them to. The book outright says that they don't bleed Vitae like they do normal blood, <i>even with blush of life active</i>. Sure, the vampire can go into the fight intending to bleed. It doesn't mean it automatically drains her Vitae to go into the werewolf when the latter bites her. The books seem to support this. You can't automatically blood bond a werewolf biting you unless the ST rules otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure most werewolves, if they know they're biting a vampire, aren't going to want anything to do with the stolen, mystical blood in their veins. If they bite, they won't be doing so with the intent to ingest anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 01-09-2016, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:22:32-08:00","id":804354,"title":"","content":"While I agree that a werewolf doesnt' have to automaticly ingest vitae when he bite someone, when you say this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804259#post804259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a vampire bites someone, whether the initial bite attack or using the Feed move, they do drain Vitae, because it's what they do. In fact, the book actually says that <i>mortals </i>take one lethal damage per Vitae taken with the Feed move, or from the 1 Vitae taken automatically (which one assumes is voluntary) when they bite someone. The same section calls out werewolves as being immune to the effects of the bite where the word &quot;mortal&quot; is used, so you could even argue that they don't take lethal damage from being drained of Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's irrelevant to the discussion at hand. Even the point about kindred not bleeding vitae is irrelevant since it was specificly mentionned that the kindred in question would consciously be bleeding vitae for the chance to be bonding the werewolf.<br /> <br /> If a kindred is being attacked by a werewolf he can decide to bleed to chance a bond. The werewolf when biting risk bonding and addiction if he swallow. Neither part of the problem are automatic and must be voluntary on both participant. The one grey area is what happen in Kuruth ?<br /> <br /> Now the real question is whether or not a werewolf can resist the bond after swallowing vitae. The section that differentiate werewolves from mortal specificly mention that it does in reference to the effect of a vampire bite. The book make no such direct allowance for resisting blood bonds. <br /> It's of course possible to argue that werewolf would get a chance to resist based on the equivalence of Primal urge and blood potency except the vampire book specificly mention that such equivalency only apply when a werewolf would resist a discipline. The werewolf book use similar language, blood potency is equivalent to primal urge for contested roll of gifts.<br /> That seems to indicate that a werewolf, or indeed any other supernatural, is just as suceptible to the blood bond as a mortal.<br /> <br /> That of course means werewolves in the know would be very careful not to swallow blood from a vampire.<br /> <br /> Mechanicly the next question is what happen when a bond is established. there should be no change when it come to the social interaction part. the question is what happens to the breaking points for causing direct or indirect harm ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:48:10-08:00","id":804364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804354#post804354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's irrelevant to the discussion at hand. Even the point about kindred not bleeding vitae is irrelevant since it was specificly mentionned that the kindred in question would consciously be bleeding vitae for the chance to be bonding the werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very relevant. It's a direct statement that vampires do not bleed normally, nor do they bleed Vitae, even when cut or suffering severe injury. The vampire's undead body works a certain way; trying to force the werewolf to drink must be a conscious act, just as it must be if the werewolf chooses for some reason to drink. My point is that it won't happen automatically based on any action either is taking. The vampire could open up a vein or allow Vitae to pour out through a wound and attempt to get the werewolf to drink it, but I don't believe the Kindred can simply choose ahead of time to bleed Vitae into a biting werewolf's mouth in response to an attack\u2014and if she can, it still does not force the werewolf to actually swallow it unless the werewolf had already intended to do so. Which she might. Play up the sweet, unnatural appeal of the stolen blood on one's tongue and maybe the character gives in because that makes sense. More likely, Rage means that the werewolf doesn't care at all and just eviscerates the vampire (since she'd have to make a Resolve + Composure roll to even choose to drink the Vitae rather than attack)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804354#post804354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one grey area is what happen in Kuruth ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here we get into Storyteller discretionary calls. I think that risk of Vinculum means nothing to a werewolf in <i>Kuruth</i>. Any attempts to influence or change the werewolf's course of action, even by supernatural means, suffer double Primal Urge as a penalty\u2014in addition to supernatural tolerance. What that means depends on the answer to the following....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804354#post804354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the real question is whether or not a werewolf can resist the bond after swallowing vitae. The section that differentiate werewolves from mortal specificly mention that it does in reference to the effect of a vampire bite. The book make no such direct allowance for resisting blood bonds.<br /> It's of course possible to argue that werewolf would get a chance to resist based on the equivalence of Primal urge and blood potency except the vampire book specificly mention that such equivalency only apply when a werewolf would resist a discipline. The werewolf book use similar language, blood potency is equivalent to primal urge for contested roll of gifts.<br /> That seems to indicate that a werewolf, or indeed any other supernatural, is just as suceptible to the blood bond as a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could the werewolf roll Primal Urge instead of Blood Potency to resist a drink adding to the blood bond? Possibly. That's a call for Storytellers to make, and probably depends on which game features your protagonists. Again, I personally don't like the idea that a werewolf is defenseless against Vinculum, so I'd allow them to resist it like vampires do, as I would for any creature with a Supernatural Tolerance trait.<br /> <br /> Now, how do we apply the <i>Kuruth </i>penalty to this particular scenario? Well, you could simply double it and add it to her normal Primal Urge rating if you allow them to roll to resist like vampires. You could apply the penalty to whatever course of action the vampire is taking to try to bond the werewolf. You could just say that Death Rage pretty much nullifies any concern of Vinculum. Or find some other ruling that your group agrees upon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804354#post804354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That of course means werewolves in the know would be very careful not to swallow blood from a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they would, anyway. In Armory: Reloaded, there was a neat little chapter fiction about that, where a werewolf met a vampire. The vampire was actually the aggressor at first, and the werewolf only had all kinds of different rumors and hearsay for reference. Turns out that he settled for a good old-fashioned punch to the jaw, but he was obviously tense and just wanted to get away. I think most werewolves would, without knowing all the details, still be hesitant at best to swallow vampire blood. If the vampire starts trying to force her to? That werewolf is going to fight very hard to make sure that it doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804354#post804354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanicly the next question is what happen when a bond is established. there should be no change when it come to the social interaction part. the question is what happens to the breaking points for causing direct or indirect harm ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wondered myself. Doing it like Integrity doesn't work, because Harmony is nothing like Integrity. Werewolf perspective is as radically alien to a normal person's as is a vampire's, or perhaps more so. If anything, I would think it a breaking point toward flesh, because that seems the most fitting. This is one of those cases where you'd have to settle on a particular ruling, whether it's a breaking point toward flesh, spirit, or doesn't affect Harmony at all.<br /> <br /> I think we could all agree on the lessons learned from this thread: werewolves shouldn't attempt to drink vampire blood ever, and vampires trying to blood bond werewolves will probably find it a lot more trouble than it's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:51:16-08:00","id":804366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804206#post804206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that clear up my stance on this matter? My earlier post inadvertently suggested that I meant you could gain Essence from blood alone; clarity is my burden (more so since I'm working on Changeling), so here I have attempted to clarify my thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your stance was always clear. The problem is that its a stance at all. Its your opinion, its your take on the issue. It is not objective fact. Individual stories have different needs. You have been presenting your stance as the only way to do it. That is what I object to. If you had the authority of a Werewolf developer, I'd listen to it as cannon. But, right now, it feels as if you're just stating an opinion.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't have an issue with an attempt to blood bond, because werewolves have a lot of ways to bolster dice pools to pretty high levels when rolling to resist - this is not automatic. Indomitable merit, Kuruth bonus, that one Gift I forget the name of, simply finish killing the vampire. And the sheer difficulty of pulling it off while surviving combat is a huge question in the first place.<br /> <br /> The Vinculum isn't all powerful. It works through social maneuvering - it gives someone a Perfect Impression, and only after a level 3 bond. The only way to establish a level 3 bond in combat is to have Coil of the Voivode 3, and you have to spend a whopping 5 vitae to use said ability, which means you're not going to be fighting back or healing effectively. That's not an insignificant investment for a vampire for putting a bond on someone and THEN still needing to spend a few turns to remove their Doors and talk a single werewolf down <i>while in the middle of combat</i>. With the werewolf's pack right there, watching, and the Cahalith likely knowing something funky going on and telling the entire pack to murder-kill the vampire messing with one of them.<br /> <br /> Yes, the blood bond has a &quot;don't attack me!&quot; clause, but that works through Humanity / Integrity breaking points. Werewolves, at worst, would suffer a breaking point towards Spirit from ignoring that compulsion. Which, frankly, is par for the course with Werewolves. It happens all the time and, honestly, you can balance that out by going out and eating pizza after the fact. At best, nothing happens.<br /> <br /> I think having the bond and addiction is dramatic, because it adds a certain level of stories after the fact. Think about it. Werewolves addicted to vitae after killing a cotorie. This is going to push the pack into hunting down more vampires, because of the addictive rush of tearing into vampires. Its a dangerous, double edged blade that threatens a wolf's balance, which is important to Werewolf stories in the first place. More drama is good. But, in mid combat, its at best a desperate act that has very little chance of success.<br /> <br /> Make no mistake, werewolves are probably the physically most competent of all supernaturals in the CoD right now. Killing on the hunt is their specialty. But mind control, drugging, and infecting others is a vampire's forte.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-09-2016, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T05:26:44-08:00","id":804385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804366#post804366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Make no mistake, werewolves are probably the physically most competent of all supernaturals in the CoD right now. Killing on the hunt is their specialty. But mind control, drugging, and infecting others is a vampire's forte.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if I understand right, some werewolf can use twice his primal urge to resist to all the mental control effect, also from disciplines...it seems that they are pretty uncontrollable also with Disciplines. So they can counter also this aspect of the vampires...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T06:13:30-08:00","id":804410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804366#post804366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your stance was always clear. The problem is that its a stance at all. Its your opinion, its your take on the issue. It is not objective fact. Individual stories have different needs. You have been presenting your stance as the only way to do it. That is what I object to. If you had the authority of a Werewolf developer, I'd listen to it as cannon. But, right now, it feels as if you're just stating an opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no objective facts to go, everyone's is an opinion, because the rulings are made on the spot, subjectively, by an ST call. So she's completely entitled to have a stance. This isn't DnD where every rule is explicitly laid there on how spells and shit interact with one another.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T06:15:06-08:00","id":804411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804385#post804385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well if I understand right, some werewolf can use twice his primal urge to resist to all the mental control effect, also from disciplines...it seems that they are pretty uncontrollable also with Disciplines. So they can counter also this aspect of the vampires...</div> </div> </div> </div>Every werewolf gets to add twice his primal Urge as penalties to being swayed or compelled while in the throes of Death Rage. On top of any rolls they get to resist said power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T07:03:13-08:00","id":804428,"title":"","content":"Some notes re werewolves and blood bonding from the Forsaken side of things:<br /> - Werewolves choose to i\u200bmbibe or consume (or not) what they bite. Bite attacks will not cause the werewolf to imbibe Vitae unless the Uratha chooses to do so (which they might do without realising the consequences if they don't know about the nature of vampire blood).<br /> - Werewolves should probably have the same ability to resist blood bonds as vampires, only using Primal Urge instead.<br /> - Note that Uratha do not suffer a Harmony breaking point for harming a regnant.<br /> - A death raging Uratha will treat a regnant no differently to any other target (although the other benefits of the blood bond, mainly the Discipline boost, will still be effective).<br /> <br /> My current thought is that an Uratha should *probably* always treat harming a regnant as a Harmony breaking point towards 5, eg a balancing breaking point. The bindings of a regnant's blood bond are an unbalancing taint and actions to break free of it are Harmonious in nature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T10:23:26-08:00","id":804528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804385#post804385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well if I understand right, some werewolf can use twice his primal urge to resist to all the mental control effect, also from disciplines...it seems that they are pretty uncontrollable also with Disciplines. So they can counter also this aspect of the vampires...</div> </div> </div> </div> Only when in Kuruth / Death Rage, which is generally during a hunt, putting us squarely back on Werewolf specialties again. Stopping the hunt is near impossible. <br /> <br /> Arrange some situation where werewolves won't be in Kuruth (ambush, somewhere crowded, etc) and the vampires have the advantage. Each splat has its strengths, and whomever can play to those strengths generally will win in any competition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T11:40:22-08:00","id":804577,"title":"","content":"Eh, Uratha can Kuruth at will with going gauru at the sightless provocation (read outside of initiatives) Siskir-Dah is optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T12:45:31-08:00","id":804630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804366#post804366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your stance was always clear. The problem is that its a stance at all. Its your opinion, its your take on the issue. It is not objective fact. Individual stories have different needs. You have been presenting your stance as the only way to do it. That is what I object to. If you had the authority of a Werewolf developer, I'd listen to it as cannon. But, right now, it feels as if you're just stating an opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of what I was saying was opinion and personal judgment calls. Some of it was just fact as stated by the books, regarding werewolves biting vampires and the consequences thereof. The rest, like if they can resist blood bonds and such, is squarely in the realm of ST calls.<br /> <br /> Regarding <i>Kuruth</i> (this isn't just you, but to everyone talking about it in the last page or so), that's generally both an &quot;I lose&quot; and an &quot;I win&quot; button combined. At that point, the finesse and skill of the sacred hunt is lost. It's a state of mindless savagery. While its ferocity and power are impressive (especially with some physical enhancement Gifts), it's also completely bereft of the nobility and spirituality that belies the hunt. It's killing for the sake of killing, without any other purpose. Going into <i>Kuruth </i>is basically losing all reasons for partaking in <i>siskur-dah</i>, so it's very much an unwanted scenario for the werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 01-09-2016, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:24:17-08:00","id":804745,"title":"","content":"Sorry my english is not the best, but what is with animalism 4 Feral Infection? Can a Vampire it not use to controll the entire Pack an let kill them each other? Even one or two can Resist the Vampire can controle the rest. Whitch Obfuscate we have some tries^^<br /> <br /> or Dominate 4 The Lying Mind the Vampire catch one Werwolfe alone whip his mind clean and tell him that we are his best Friends an the other (his Pack Members) Killd his Familly, or so something.<br /> <br /> or other Forms of Animalism summon a entire rat army and let them fight (maby the Werwolfs think we are such Rat Spirits (Beshilu ?)<br /> <br /> or Protean 3 with swarm Form^^ (Rat) or Raven Fligh -&gt; Attack -&gt; Fligh-&gt; Attack = OK they will not win but my Vampire will have a lot of Fun<br /> <br /> or Protan 4 with Wings he flies over the Werwolf drobs Molotowcoctails or Bombs or Eggs or something.^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6981-lukrasis","user":"lukrasis","date":". 01-09-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6981-lukrasis","name":"lukrasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:53:26-08:00","id":804773,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with a vampire trying to direct a werewolf in Kuruth to kill their own pack is that it would require a werewolf in Kuruth to be able to <i>recognise</i> their own pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T15:55:21-08:00","id":804774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lukrasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804745#post804745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry my english is not the best, but what is with animalism 4 Feral Infection? Can a Vampire it not use to controll the entire Pack an let kill them each other? Even one or two can Resist the Vampire can controle the rest. Whitch Obfuscate we have some tries^^</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use it to send an entire pack into frenzy, yes. The victims can spend Willpower to resist the vampire's command, but they're still frenzied. They'll attack anyone except for other werewolves in <i>Kuruth </i>(Death Rage), so if the vampire successfully manages to frenzy most or all of the pack, well ... now you have a bunch of Death Raging werewolves who all want you in pieces and are very difficult to control even for supernatural powers. If only some succumb, yes, that's chaos, and the werewolves are probably going to kill each other (unless the rest frenzy as well). Either way, if I am that vampire, I'd want to get away as soon as possible and let the chaos unfold from a safe distance.<br /> <br /> Welcome to the forum!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T16:13:23-08:00","id":804782,"title":"","content":"save distant?^^ lets change in a Bird. Vampire can use her Disciplins (B&amp;S). No one note the bad birdy over the heads. (I Imagine jumping werwolfs to catch the Bird^^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6981-lukrasis","name":"lukrasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T16:19:03-08:00","id":804785,"title":"","content":"Unless one of them knows Scent of the Unnatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T16:25:19-08:00","id":804786,"title":"","content":"They always have to catch the Bird^^ (or Birds/ Swarm Form)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6981-lukrasis","name":"lukrasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T18:17:31-08:00","id":804878,"title":"","content":"Tongue of Flame is just what the doctor prescribed for vermin, spiritual or blood-sucking alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T01:57:33-08:00","id":805083,"title":"","content":"Do the Werewolves have a response to the range advantage offered by Blood Sorcery? Getting a spell out to a couple of miles isn't <i>that</i> difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T02:21:36-08:00","id":805091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=805083#post805083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Werewolves have a response to the range advantage offered by Blood Sorcery? Getting a spell out to a couple of miles isn't <i>that</i> difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves have very few &quot;ranged attack&quot; Gifts/Rites and most of those they have access to that work sympathetically are aimed at pack mates or targets of <i>Siskur-Dah.</i><br /> <br /> Whether they can notice when they are a target of Blood Sorcery is a bit of an ST call. The feeling Kindred targets of Blood Sorcery get is likened to Blood Sympathy, which werewolves definitely do not profit from, but the actual description also invokes the idea of the Predatory Aura of the sorcerer being carried through their sorcery. In a Chronicle in which werewolves can sense the Predatory Aura without the aid of physical signs, on an entirely mystic level, you could make an argument they would feel it, but probably have no way of interpreting exactly what is happening or what they should do.<br /> <br /> I could imagine some spirits or werewolves experienced in dealing with vampires could teach a Rite that allows them to pick up on it, including the ability to track the sorcerer like a vampire can, but I think it would be fairly rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:18:50-08:00","id":805113,"title":"","content":"Catastrophe. That has an area of effect centred on the werewolf with a radius of twice their glory renown in miles. It's a bit overkill, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T05:59:14-08:00","id":805180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=805083#post805083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Werewolves have a response to the range advantage offered by Blood Sorcery? Getting a spell out to a couple of miles isn't <i>that</i> difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Glory Facet of Warding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T06:11:12-08:00","id":805190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=805113#post805113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Catastrophe. That has an area of effect centred on the werewolf with a radius of twice their glory renown in miles. It's a bit overkill, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it is also pretty indiscriminate. It does not read like you can target the Influence like &quot;fuck up these walking leeches only&quot;, so you have no guarantee they get ashed before they get the fuck out of dodge with Celerity or frenzy once things start randomly combusting all around them. Unless the werewolf has like Glory 4 and Purity 4 at which point I imagine they can unleash a literal biblical firestorm. Of course, if a couple city blocks are turned to ash in an instant, like a moment out of Revelation, you would imagine some people and powers would take note. It would be cool as a final &quot;Fuck You!&quot; after defeat is clear, but that is hard when 1 roll is already an hour.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=805180#post805180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Glory Facet of Warding.</div> </div> </div> </div>ST call at best, I would say. It only talks of various kinds of breeches, including scrying windows. Sure, that would probably apply to any kind of divination attempts, but Blood Sorcery curses and whatnot work by pure sympathy. There is no &quot;gateway&quot; or &quot;opening&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":".  Replied to Ephsy 01-10-2016, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T06:30:44-08:00","id":805197,"title":"","content":"A werewolf could use Pack Kin to induct a small predatory bird into their pack, then Beast Ride to borrow it's body, and then Reflected Facets to use their powers through it in a moderately covert fashion. That has a maximum range of five miles, because it's based on Cunning score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T06:34:51-08:00","id":805198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=805190#post805190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ST call at best, I would say. It only talks of various kinds of breeches, including scrying windows. Sure, that would probably apply to any kind of divination attempts, but Blood Sorcery curses and whatnot work by pure sympathy. There is no &quot;gateway&quot; or &quot;opening&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, everything is an ST call. How do you think sympathy works in Mage? Similar systems, similar applications. So yeah, your magic needs a gateway to work remotely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-10-2016, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T06:36:14-08:00","id":805201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=805198#post805198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, everything is an ST call. How do you think sympathy works in Mage? Similar systems, similar applications.</div> </div> </div> </div>And still we sit here! You are right of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T07:52:11-08:00","id":805238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=805113#post805113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Catastrophe. That has an area of effect centred on the werewolf with a radius of twice their glory renown in miles. It's a bit overkill, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with Catastrophe is that using it is going to piss off every other supernatural critter in the region, and that's how you end up deader than dead really really quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T07:56:32-08:00","id":805243,"title":"","content":"Yeah but at least you 'won'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:10:34-08:00","id":806020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=805083#post805083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Werewolves have a response to the range advantage offered by Blood Sorcery? Getting a spell out to a couple of miles isn't <i>that</i> difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless we're using Blood Sorcery rules (which I don't consider a given), Blood Sorcery has a range of a single mile and a casting time of at least an hour. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=805091#post805091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In a Chronicle in which werewolves can sense the Predatory Aura without the aid of physical signs, on an entirely mystic level, you could make an argument they would feel it, but probably have no way of interpreting exactly what is happening or what they should do.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interestingly, this is an area where, by default, vampires hold an advantage over the werewolves. The wolves have no way to detect vampires without specific Gifts (Scent the Unnatural and Boundary Ward, both with sharp restrictions), while vampires can tell a werewolf instantly from their aura. Vampires always know when another predator is around, while werewolves senses tend to be focused on the Hisil more than fleshy beings.<br /> <br /> That said, there IS a proto-Tribe in the Werewolf book who thinks that they should have vampires as their Sacred Prey, so they might have some tricks up their furry arms. But that is firmly up in homebrew territory, so not much we can say here will help if that's the case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=804630#post804630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding <i>Kuruth</i> (this isn't just you, but to everyone talking about it in the last page or so), that's generally both an &quot;I lose&quot; and an &quot;I win&quot; button combined. At that point, the finesse and skill of the sacred hunt is lost. It's a state of mindless savagery. While its ferocity and power are impressive (especially with some physical enhancement Gifts), it's also completely bereft of the nobility and spirituality that belies the hunt. It's killing for the sake of killing, without any other purpose. Going into <i>Kuruth </i>is basically losing all reasons for partaking in <i>siskur-dah</i>, so it's very much an unwanted scenario for the werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wish that was true. For all that the some attempt to convey that its a Bad Thing, generally speaking, I feel more like the book conveyed it as a tactical consideration than something that's automatically bad. You don't shoot grenades off in crowded areas, but if you've isolated the prey, like a good wolf pack is supposed to do? What reason is there not to use the heavy weaponry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:21:09-08:00","id":806023,"title":"","content":"I never got the impression that vampires could auto-sense werewolves. In fact, I think this sort of flies in the face of the entire point of Hishu form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:47:27-08:00","id":806035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806023#post806023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got the impression that vampires could auto-sense werewolves. In fact, I think this sort of flies in the face of the entire point of Hishu form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They do, they basically get scared. It is in the side bar near predatory aura, pg 92. It is an &quot;Oh shit, looking at this guy makes me want to run or shit myself&quot; sensation when they spot them. Works same way they detect vampires, basically werewolves have a predatory aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:49:52-08:00","id":806037,"title":"","content":"That's <i>after</i> they notice werewolves. More of a dawning realization than a werewolf detector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:04:36-08:00","id":806046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806023#post806023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got the impression that vampires could auto-sense werewolves. In fact, I think this sort of flies in the face of the entire point of Hishu form.</div> </div> </div> </div> Others and the Predatory Aura sidebar, p92, specifically states that when a Kindred interacts with a werewolf, they get the feelings they normally wouldn't experience. Vampires can theoretically detect others as well, though that's up to ST discretion.<br /> <br /> Hishu, as per the rules on WtF p96, just inflicts a penalty to pursuit or trying to pinpoint, not general detection. The point is to evade pursuit, or avoid being picked out of crowd. Predatory Aura works once you've already spotted the werewolf, and you recognize him as a fellow predator when face to face. The two abilities operate on different wavelengths. Even then, hishu doesn't negate any attempt to sense them, its only a <i>penalty, </i>which is an odd thing to reconcile with a power that auto-succeeds. Even if you want to argue that the innate ability of one supernatural is clashing with the innate ability of another, that'd be a Clash of Wills roll that the wolf remains unaware of if he loses. It is still a situation that favors the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:19:38-08:00","id":806055,"title":"","content":"Well, either way you've still neglected the fact that a werewolf's senses are sharp enough that they'd probably pick up on the lack of breathing or a heartbeat, or that the vamp didn't smell right, or a bunch of other tells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:23:31-08:00","id":806059,"title":"","content":"Apparently most vampires neglect their dental hygiene, so blood breath is a common indicator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:27:39-08:00","id":806062,"title":"","content":"Let me give an exmaple of how I see the two of them (hishu form and pred aura) working. <br /> <br /> Imagine vampire A, B, C, D, and E are all from different clans, and are at a bar discussing the latest moves by their rivals from other covenants. Five werewolves, one of the so-called twice-blessed pack, walk into the bar, all in Hishu form. The vampires would suffer a penalty (-Primal Urge) to actually NOTICE the wolves coming in. The vamps wouldn't really pay the wolves any mind. And, if you don't notice someone, then Pred Aura doesn't trigger. The two groups, oblivious to each other, go on their night, both blending in to humanity in general. <br /> <br /> The wolves, however, came here to hunt down one of their prey - the Storm Lord of the group tracked one of the Claimed to this bar. And, once they found him, the werewolves confront him. Start drawing attention to themselves. At this point, all eyes in the bar are shiting to the wolves and the Claimed. You can't really not notice and pinpoint the wolves, even with a penalty. They're the center of attention. At this point, the vamps take a good look at the wolves, and -now- Predatory Aura triggers. As a group, the vamps stiffen, and quietly exit the bar.<br /> <br /> The next night, ABCD and E go back to the same bar, and try to glance around for the werewolves again. Vamprie E, a Mehket, even uses Auspex. Each vampire suffers -PU to detect the pack quietly sitting in the corner, they just blend in. Three of the vamps fail to notice. E's Auspex dice pool is penalized, and bad luck causes her to fail as well. Vamp A gets lucky and rolls a 10 on a chance die, spotting the pack and immediately feeling the auras again once she does. The cotorie leaves the bar again.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, having noticed that group walk out both times they spotted the pack, decide to investigate. They get up, and as a group in Hishu, follow. The vampires suffer PU as a penalty to notice they're being followed through a crowd. A few blocks, the crowd thins, and the pack stands out. Predatory Aura triggers again once they're spotted.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:30:02-08:00","id":806063,"title":"","content":"I think either Rose or Charlaquin or somebody said that vamps and werewolves recognize each other pretty quickly. They're both apex predators with heightened physical and supernatural senses. The metaphor I remember somebody using was that they're like secret agents working in the same city: They recognize the spycraft that the other is using, and that they can tell that they're aware of each other. They keep an eye on each other, give each other knowing glances when they randomly pass on the street.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:31:34-08:00","id":806064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806055#post806055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, either way you've still neglected the fact that a werewolf's senses are sharp enough that they'd probably pick up on the lack of breathing or a heartbeat, or that the vamp didn't smell right, or a bunch of other tells.</div> </div> </div> </div> 1) there's no rules for that, and using it that way is specifically negating the whole point of Sense the Unnatrual Gift. If you make that call, you are making a house rule. 2) Blush of Life negates the lack of heartbeat, and vamps breathe - otherwise, how else would they talk or smell things? 3) A clean vampire tends to smell like a normal human. Humans are a combination of all the scents we run into on a daily basis. Our clothes, the dirt, our soap, our family and friends. Maybe a bit of blood, but then, that could just mean someone got into a fight or worked in a blood clinic. 4) Picking all that out of a scent requires you to be pretty damn close and actually LOOK for it. Its not on the same level as Pred Aura either.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scent of the Unnatrual and Boundary Ward are the only two abilities that I'm aware of that can actually detect a vampire. Nothing in the book suggests otherwise. If you are assuming otherwise, that's got to be a house call, and not an official rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-11-2016, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T07:38:34-08:00","id":806070,"title":"","content":"We've been mostly identifying people through Know Thy Prey.<br /> <br /> There's a few other abilities that let you notice and identify supernaturals, Scent of the Unnatural, one of the Warding ones.<br /> <br /> Know Thy Prey tells you every name they're known by, as well as their Status, Retainer, Allies and Contact merits. After our first experience with vampires we hung out and got as much information on their society as possible, though we neglected their powers and weaknesses, and so we recognize the terms used across the various covenants, and the names of the covenants themselves.<br /> <br /> We've identified a couple hunters through similar methods. But the local hunter compact has a very obvious name so we didn't have to do as much investigation.<br /> <br /> Also, ghouls tend to be identifiable by scent, just being in the same room of them gives a particular odor to the area. Though pinpointing it can be difficult, especially if they have Obfuscation. As a side note, this may just be a regional thing, the vampires are centrally located in certain areas with distinct scents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-11-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:04:29-08:00","id":806088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806064#post806064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> using it that way is specifically negating the whole point of Sense the Unnatrual Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't. Scent the unnatural is a radar effect. I was talking up close and personal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:24:56-08:00","id":806099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806088#post806088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it isn't. Scent the unnatural is a radar effect. I was talking up close and personal.</div> </div> </div> </div> And why are you up close and personal and smelling someone? Why approach a vampire in the first place? If you're on the hunt with a vampire as prey, then yes, you're likely to figure it out. Werewolves are the ultimate in hunting, and can figure out a hell of a lot when they bring their resources to bear. A casual meet and greet? Two souls that happen to meet in a bar? Not as much. Why accuse me of ignoring it when it requires such a specific, contrived white-room-ish scenario? Its still nothing even remotely resembling what vampires can do with Predatory Aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:36:10-08:00","id":806106,"title":"","content":"Considering a werewolf in Hishu can have incredible pin-pointing hearing for miles and miles without being penalized by ambient sound, yeah, that dude without the heartbeat? pretty damned fishy.<br /> <br /> I never needed White Wolf to spell out every roll for me, and I'm not gonna start asking them now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T08:44:00-08:00","id":806117,"title":"","content":"They're kind of like Daredevil, with their senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:26:45-08:00","id":806210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806106#post806106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering a werewolf in Hishu can have incredible pin-pointing hearing for miles and miles without being penalized by ambient sound, yeah, that dude without the heartbeat? pretty damned fishy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the fact that...you know....that's not at all what the book says.<br /> Wolf sense in Hishu form ? not automatic, conscious choice. Second hearing range is for several miles except in a city it's limited to immediate surroundings. Nigh impossible to pinpoint any single source so listening for the heartbeat of lack thereof of a vampire is simply not possible outside of wildly improbable scenarios were the vampire is alone in the wild.<br /> <br /> But frankly I expect little else from crossover threads, they always devolve into pissing contest with wild claims that have little to do with actual rules just as long as they support whatever splat people like best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T11:39:39-08:00","id":806281,"title":"","content":"Vampires come out when it's dark. Wolf senses help you see in the dark. Ergo, vampires are around at the time a werewolf is most likely to be running around with their wolf senses on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:12:15-08:00","id":806311,"title":"","content":"You know, I was going to respond, but Elderand is right. The prejudice and biases are too strong to bother with anything approaching realistic games or depictations. I'm out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:18:13-08:00","id":806316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806064#post806064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scent of the Unnatrual and Boundary Ward are the only two abilities that I'm aware of that can actually detect a vampire. Nothing in the book suggests otherwise. If you are assuming otherwise, that's got to be a house call, and not an official rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E, werewolves could get a sense of a vampire not being quite right through smell alone. Without blush of life active, they don't give off their natural bodily scents. They smell like old, dried blood and similar unpleasant things. This may still hold true in second edition since that's really just the way heightened senses of smell and hearing work. Yes, the werewolf would have to get close to be sure, but if a vampire doesn't have blush of life active, any werewolf using wolf senses is going to quickly realize that there's something off about the vampire. Scent the Unnatural is better for detecting these things, but the werewolf isn't blind without it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:23:48-08:00","id":806320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806020#post806020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish that was true. For all that the some attempt to convey that its a Bad Thing, generally speaking, I feel more like the book conveyed it as a tactical consideration than something that's automatically bad. You don't shoot grenades off in crowded areas, but if you've isolated the prey, like a good wolf pack is supposed to do? What reason is there not to use the heavy weaponry?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think because <i>Gauru </i>is heavy enough. You're still (mostly) in control. <i>Kuruth </i>means you'll attack anyone, packmates included, if they don't join you in mindless rage. Not a good thing. And depending on how long it lasts, a whole pack of remorseless killers loping off after the kill to find more things to eviscerate is also very bad. You don't know what you have done until you come out of it sometime later, and may have left a trail of blood behind you. That's how you end up being hunted by enemies you didn't know you had, or draw the attention of werewolf hunters, and things like that. <i>Kuruth </i>does offer some pretty serious benefits (especially with any physical Gifts), but I think the total loss of control and the potential loss of Harmony are significant enough drawbacks that I'd avoid <i>Kuruth </i>every time if I could.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's not always so easy. Peter, one of the werewolves in the fiction piece I wrote for the <i>Idigam Chronicles Anthology</i>, ended up getting himself in some very big trouble when he tried to escape his packmates during <i>Wasu-Im</i>. Such is the tragedy of Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:39:29-08:00","id":806335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806210#post806210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for the fact that...you know....that's not at all what the book says.<br /> Wolf sense in Hishu form ? not automatic, conscious choice. Second hearing range is for several miles except in a city it's limited to immediate surroundings. Nigh impossible to pinpoint any single source so listening for the heartbeat of lack thereof of a vampire is simply not possible outside of wildly improbable scenarios were the vampire is alone in the wild.<br /> <br /> But frankly I expect little else from crossover threads, they always devolve into pissing contest with wild claims that have little to do with actual rules just as long as they support whatever splat people like best.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Switching from Hishu to wolf senses is reflexive, yes, it is a conscious choice.<br /> 2) Immediate surroundings that you'll say are what? meters away? Please. If you're in a restaurant lobby with a vampire in the a nearby table, I'm damned well going to notice the lack of a pulse, if I know what I'm looking for,<br /> <br /> You're the only one who's calling wildly improbable scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:51:25-08:00","id":806349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806335#post806335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> if I know what I'm looking for</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of something exactly falls into this. Among all the other sounds in a restaurant, your noticing something missing automatically is a big difference from actively looking. And I think that is what the conversational dissonance is coming down to right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:13:20-08:00","id":806386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=803750#post803750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't blood bond a werewolf biting you. There is a huge difference between a werewolf biting, and digesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If vamp can bond or ghoul someone by spittng in the eye(example from blood Smoke) then yes the Vamps ghouls a wolf that biting them.<br /> <br /> Onto other things OP needs to look at tenebrous blood from the book of spirits. There have been a few attempts to update for second edition.<br /> Barrier of Blood should work on weres. Spirit Cruac from the Crone book.5 level 2nd ed Animalism 5th lever 2nd ed Obfuscate.<br /> BTW do you allow Dynamic blood sorcery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:14:40-08:00","id":806390,"title":"","content":"It's as they've said. You wont even have a chance to notice unless you use your Wolf Senses, but you wouldn't have a reason to use your Wolf Senses unless you've already noticed. So unless you're constantly using your Wolf Senses 24/7, which is unlikely regardless of whether or not it only takes a reflexive action, you're only likely to notice if you get lucky or if someone or somethings given you other reasons to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:17:38-08:00","id":806399,"title":"","content":"While using them 24/7 is unlikely, unless someone sticks to wolf forms, it's not uncommon among the players I've seen to activate them repeatedly throughout the day, the same way someone may take in new surroundings or check out a newcomer to a room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:27:05-08:00","id":806406,"title":"","content":"In 1e, my high PU character would have paid to be in Dalu all day, just for the sense boost. That's no longer a requirement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:27:32-08:00","id":806408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806399#post806399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While using them 24/7 is unlikely, unless someone sticks to wolf forms, it's not uncommon among the players I've seen to activate them repeatedly throughout the day, the same way someone may take in new surroundings or check out a newcomer to a room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is still just taking a random occasional shot in the dark. And if someone took a moment to check literally everybody that comes into their sensory range I'd consider that particular person in question highly, <i>highly</i> paranoid. Almost unrealistically so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 01-11-2016, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:29:43-08:00","id":806412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806390#post806390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's as they've said. You wont even have a chance to notice unless you use your Wolf Senses, but you wouldn't have a reason to use your Wolf Senses unless you've already noticed. So unless you're constantly using your Wolf Senses 24/7, which is unlikely regardless of whether or not it only takes a reflexive action, you're only likely to notice if you get lucky or if someone or somethings given you other reasons to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, I'd venture that most werewolves use Wolf Senses pretty much constantly. Even (or especially) in <i>Hishu </i>form, why would you go relatively blind to so many facets of the world when you've had a taste of true apex predator's senses? If humans are sensory dullards by comparison, and werewolves realize just how potent their senses really are after the First Change, I'm guessing most would keep them active all the time or close to it. I know my characters certainly do\u2014it's too powerful of an ability, too intrinsic to the wolf's nature, to avoid it. Your Wolf Senses literally allow you to compensate for blindness or deafness with no penalty at all, because all your senses are so greatly heightened. Even in a city, you might not be able to focus on much besides your immediate surroundings, but why miss out on all that information?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:42:02-08:00","id":806429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806412#post806412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the contrary, I'd venture that most werewolves use Wolf Senses pretty much constantly. Even (or especially) in <i>Hishu </i>form, why would you go relatively blind to so many facets of the world when you've had a taste of true apex predator's senses? If humans are sensory dullards by comparison, and werewolves realize just how potent their senses really are after the First Change, I'm guessing most would keep them active all the time or close to it. I know my characters certainly do\u2014it's too powerful of an ability, too intrinsic to the wolf's nature, to avoid it. Your Wolf Senses literally allow you to compensate for blindness or deafness with no penalty at all, because all your senses are so greatly heightened. Even in a city, you might not be able to focus on much besides your immediate surroundings, but why miss out on all that information?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's pretty unrealistic. We're getting into the all seeing mage situation in which someone is so paranoid that they are constantly loaded down with every perceptive ability/contingency known to man just because they can. It might be reflexive, but it still takes conscious effort. How many people do you know looks to every single person, place, or thing that comes into their field of view? I'd say that sensing things is no more 'intrinsic' to werewolves as looking at things is to people, but I'd wager you wouldn't know of anyone that obsessed with doing so, because while it's reflexive, it would be extremely mentally exhausting trying to keep track of everything.<br /> <br /> That said, I doubt you agree with me, and probably have some sort of reasoning as to why you do that I further disagree with so we'll just agree to disagree on this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:48:06-08:00","id":806436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806210#post806210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for the fact that...you know....that's not at all what the book says.<br /> Wolf sense in Hishu form ? not automatic, conscious choice. Second hearing range is for several miles except in a city it's limited to immediate surroundings. Nigh impossible to pinpoint any single source so listening for the heartbeat of lack thereof of a vampire is simply not possible outside of wildly improbable scenarios were the vampire is alone in the wild.<br /> <br /> But frankly I expect little else from crossover threads, they always devolve into pissing contest with wild claims that have little to do with actual rules just as long as they support whatever splat people like best.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't understand. Werewolves are the elves of the World of Darkness!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:12:40-08:00","id":806455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806436#post806436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't understand. Werewolves are the elves of the World of Darkness!</div> </div> </div> </div>Beard-capable elves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:18:07-08:00","id":806459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806429#post806429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's pretty unrealistic. We're getting into the all seeing mage situation in which someone is so paranoid that they are constantly loaded down with every perceptive ability/contingency known to man just because they can. It might be reflexive, but it still takes conscious effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it in any way unrealistic? Besides, of course, involving werewolves and supernatural senses. It's not necessarily the same thing as a mage scanning the world with Mage Sight. This is instinctive as much as it is anything else. The wolf uses its senses to examine the world in details human senses simply cannot match. They do it by instinct and by necessity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806429#post806429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people do you know looks to every single person, place, or thing that comes into their field of view? I'd say that sensing things is no more 'intrinsic' to werewolves as looking at things is to people, but I'd wager you wouldn't know of anyone that obsessed with doing so, because while it's reflexive, it would be extremely mentally exhausting trying to keep track of everything.<br /> <br /> That said, I doubt you agree with me, and probably have some sort of reasoning as to why you do that I further disagree with so we'll just agree to disagree on this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at a wolf, or even a dog. Do they not perk up their ears at every interesting sound? Always investigate every new smell? Sensing things is so very much intrinsic to werewolf life that I'm somewhat surprised you could suggest otherwise. It's not an obsession. It's an instinct. A need. Werewolves do not go blind to facets of the world humans don't even perceive. The books even talk about how much things change thanks to lupine senses compared to the average city-dweller's life. A werewolf doesn't necessarily focus on every single thing that pings one of their senses, because nothing does that. But to think that they don't use them all the time to glean a much deeper, more holistic picture of the world is very much against my reading of the books.<br /> <br /> I suppose the disconnect might come from the idea of a werewolf being overwhelmed by sensory input. I don't think they would be, even in a city. You just have to filter out the inputs that are relevant now. But because they're used to that stream of sensory details that no human can even imagine, they don't get overwhelmed by ordinary situations. Only very specifically harmful ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 01-11-2016, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:53:09-08:00","id":806539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806459#post806459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is it in any way unrealistic? Besides, of course, involving werewolves and supernatural senses. It's not necessarily the same thing as a mage scanning the world with Mage Sight. This is instinctive as much as it is anything else. The wolf uses its senses to examine the world in details human senses simply cannot match. They do it by instinct and by necessity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Look at a wolf, or even a dog. Do they not perk up their ears at every interesting sound? Always investigate every new smell? Sensing things is so very much intrinsic to werewolf life that I'm somewhat surprised you could suggest otherwise. It's not an obsession. It's an instinct. A need. Werewolves do not go blind to facets of the world humans don't even perceive. The books even talk about how much things change thanks to lupine senses compared to the average city-dweller's life. A werewolf doesn't necessarily focus on every single thing that pings one of their senses, because nothing does that. But to think that they don't use them all the time to glean a much deeper, more holistic picture of the world is very much against my reading of the books.<br /> <br /> I suppose the disconnect might come from the idea of a werewolf being overwhelmed by sensory input. I don't think they would be, even in a city. You just have to filter out the inputs that are relevant now. But because they're used to that stream of sensory details that no human can even imagine, they don't get overwhelmed by ordinary situations. Only very specifically harmful ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'll just say what I said last post, we'll have to agree to disagree because I think you're wrong, and I don't really care enough to devote the energy necessary to explain why I think you're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T16:39:08-08:00","id":806562,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806062#post806062\">MCN's scenario</a> was pretty on the ball. Providing neither side was actively looking for each other, in a crowded place it's entirely likely they could walk past each other without noticing.<br /> <br /> Especially considering it's a bar and presumably most of the group has their Blush of Life active, so they have a normal heartbeat and it isn't a quintet of pale, emaciated corpses staring without blinking at throbbing jugulars and flinching from nearby flames, and the werewolves aren't a trio in dalu walking a wolf and a particularly large wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-11-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T20:22:20-08:00","id":806709,"title":"","content":"I consider how often I use wolf senses in games to be a pretty good gauge for how often a werewolf might use them in daily life.<br /> <br /> It's pretty frequent. Pretty much anytime something catches my eye.<br /> <br /> Oh, that guy is staring at me. Does he smell like another werewolf? Wolf senses.<br /> Oh that guy is isn't meeting my eyes. Wolf senses. Why's his heart beating so fast? I can smell him sweating in his shirt. Does he know me somehow? Does he know what I am?<br /> Oh, the boisterous conversation turned to hushed whispers as I came in the room? Wolf senses. Oh, they're just racist.<br /> Oh that guy bolted as soon as I turned my back. Where's he headed? Should I follow him? Wolf senses. Oh, he's just throwing up in the alley.<br /> <br /> So I'm not saying you're gonna know anytime a vampire is around, but wolf senses are pretty reflexive (literally, I mean) so it's gonna happen sometimes for sure.<br /> <br /> I also think this is a matter of two conflicting priorities. Hishu is the form that hides the werewolf, a vampire probably shouldn't be able to instantly sense a werewolf in Hishu, that doesn't gel with the role Hishu plays in Werewolf. But the story is a bit different in Vampire (which was made without any knowledge of what Werewolf would do with Hishu) It's a game where Predatory Auras play a huge role, and they're violent, instinctive and automatic.<br /> <br /> So I'd say if you're playing a Vampire game, let vampires sense werewolves the way the book describes. That is cool and terrifying and offers a lot room to play with werewolf encounters in your campaign. If you're playing Werewolf, though, then having a major splat instantly see through what is supposed to be one of your defenses would obviously not be operating as the rules intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 01-12-2016, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:55:51-08:00","id":806765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806539#post806539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I'll just say what I said last post, we'll have to agree to disagree because I think you're wrong, and I don't really care enough to devote the energy necessary to explain why I think you're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I suggest you stop posting altogether if you aren't going to add to the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T21:57:40-08:00","id":806769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806562#post806562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806062#post806062\">MCN's scenario</a> was pretty on the ball. Providing neither side was actively looking for each other, in a crowded place it's entirely likely they could walk past each other without noticing.<br /> <br /> Especially considering it's a bar and presumably most of the group has their Blush of Life active, so they have a normal heartbeat and it isn't a quintet of pale, emaciated corpses staring without blinking at throbbing jugulars and flinching from nearby flames, and the werewolves aren't a trio in dalu walking a wolf and a particularly large wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canines can literally tell what you last ate based on your scent. The last time you went to the bathroom. The last time you took a shit. That 200 year old ancillae with a heartbeat is gonna smell like he's got the mother of all constipations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T22:32:42-08:00","id":806785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806709#post806709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider how often I use wolf senses in games to be a pretty good gauge for how often a werewolf might use them in daily life.<br /> <br /> It's pretty frequent. Pretty much anytime something catches my eye.<br /> <br /> Oh, that guy is staring at me. Does he smell like another werewolf? Wolf senses.<br /> Oh that guy is isn't meeting my eyes. Wolf senses. Why's his heart beating so fast? I can smell him sweating in his shirt. Does he know me somehow? Does he know what I am?<br /> Oh, the boisterous conversation turned to hushed whispers as I came in the room? Wolf senses. Oh, they're just racist.<br /> Oh that guy bolted as soon as I turned my back. Where's he headed? Should I follow him? Wolf senses. Oh, he's just throwing up in the alley.<br /> <br /> So I'm not saying you're gonna know anytime a vampire is around, but wolf senses are pretty reflexive (literally, I mean) so it's gonna happen sometimes for sure.<br /> <br /> I also think this is a matter of two conflicting priorities. Hishu is the form that hides the werewolf, a vampire probably shouldn't be able to instantly sense a werewolf in Hishu, that doesn't gel with the role Hishu plays in Werewolf. But the story is a bit different in Vampire (which was made without any knowledge of what Werewolf would do with Hishu) It's a game where Predatory Auras play a huge role, and they're violent, instinctive and automatic.<br /> <br /> So I'd say if you're playing a Vampire game, let vampires sense werewolves the way the book describes. That is cool and terrifying and offers a lot room to play with werewolf encounters in your campaign. If you're playing Werewolf, though, then having a major splat instantly see through what is supposed to be one of your defenses would obviously not be operating as the rules intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>While tone plays a part in how people interpret things. As someone who played and live through the WoD's, &quot;Kill it! It's EEEV-UL!&quot; once with Garou and fully experienced all the trouble and horror it was trying to cross over WtA with Vampire mechanically and narratively. Things that smack of that same approach turn me off rather fast because they smack far more to me of mascot wars than they do in the endeavor of telling a particular compelling story. There is a relationship between mechanics and being able to get immersed into a setting and I get that. But that's never stopped these types of conversations to almost always be little more than people trying to find a way to &quot;win&quot; the &quot;game&quot; or prove some other sort of superiority over what someone else might like more rather than dealing with how does any particular part of either game allow or hinder making an interest keeping story for the players. Mach 7 Uratha? That's going to up there with a lot of stuff that would completely kill the vibe of what the eerie Twilight Zone meets cosmic horror meets primal horror meets, etc,etc that is the ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T01:56:26-08:00","id":806852,"title":"","content":"Well, if the game, like the OP described it was &quot;How easy it is to fuck with Uratha as vampires?&quot;, this is what you get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T03:02:16-08:00","id":806868,"title":"","content":"In situations like this, I tend to follow the 'Protagonists rule'. Briefly, rule in favour of the protagonist. In a Vampire game, it's more likely that the vamps will notice the werewolves and be able to use their Disciplines to hide/escape/defeat them.<br /> <br /> In a werewolf game, the wolves are more likely to notice/track/hunt the vampires. <br /> <br /> Use all the same rules, just give slightly more weight to the protagonists. (This being a Vampire thread, I'd suggest the bloodsuckers have the edge.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T03:15:45-08:00","id":806871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806868#post806868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In situations like this, I tend to follow the 'Protagonists rule'. Briefly, rule in favour of the protagonist. In a Vampire game, it's more likely that the vamps will notice the werewolves and be able to use their Disciplines to hide/escape/defeat them.<br /> <br /> In a werewolf game, the wolves are more likely to notice/track/hunt the vampires.<br /> <br /> Use all the same rules, just give slightly more weight to the protagonists. (This being a Vampire thread, I'd suggest the bloodsuckers have the edge.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one go with the &quot;Story rule&quot;.<br /> I'll give the edge to whichever side makes the most interesting story.<br /> <br /> I admit that this has downsides, though. When the story in a following chapter has different themes, the need to stay consistent can make things annoying and/or awkward.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T03:42:39-08:00","id":806882,"title":"","content":"You could also turn it around for an &quot;antagonist rule&quot;. Always go with what makes the antagonist a scarier and fiercer opponent. After all, fearsome opponents make for good stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T03:48:42-08:00","id":806886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806765#post806765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then I suggest you stop posting altogether if you aren't going to add to the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what you're doing right here? Except your post is even less relevant because at the very least I was expressing an opinion on the topic at hand. What are <i>you</i> adding to this discussion with this post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:44:12-08:00","id":806910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806882#post806882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also turn it around for an &amp;quot;antagonist rule&amp;quot;. Always go with what makes the antagonist a scarier and fiercer opponent. After all, fearsome opponents make for good stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fearsome opponents that the players feel they have a chance of defeating make even better stories! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T04:54:23-08:00","id":806916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806886#post806886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like what you're doing right here? Except your post is even less relevant because at the very least I was expressing an opinion on the topic at hand. What are <i>you</i> adding to this discussion with this post?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not repeating myself, and directly below that post is another post I made. But guess you glossed it over given you don't have any stake here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T05:06:15-08:00","id":806920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806910#post806910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fearsome opponents that the players feel they have a chance of defeating make even better stories! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pish posh! All these modern RPGs with their player coddling and hand-holding mechanics! I remember a time when surviving a session was a challenge and you had a bucket list of spare character sheets you brought to every session! Youngsters with their &quot;Ooooh, but dying every session is no fun! How can there be a proper character arc? Ooooh! Woe is me! You are so mean Mr. Dungeon Master!&quot;, what we need is some proper Tomb of Horrors ... filled with Horrors! If I did not get my allotted tribute of blood, sweat and tears, how do I know I did my job right?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This is a joke</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T05:35:16-08:00","id":806933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806916#post806916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not repeating myself, and directly below that post is another post I made. But guess you glossed it over given you don't have any stake here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Directly below it, so not part of the post in question. So you spent a stand alone post to point out that someone shouldn't disagree unless they were willing to argue over it for an additional 20 thread pages. And disagreeing is showing that you have a stake in it, it is important to know where people stand on various issues, even if they don't feel like composing a 6 paragraph response detailing with exact quotes why someone is wrong. I made my point, sure, yet it was apparently misunderstood since the argument was carried on afterwards regardless, necessitating my need to restate that I wasn't going to bother arguing that specific point even though I explicitly disagreed with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T06:44:38-08:00","id":806967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806933#post806933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Directly below it, so not part of the post in question. So you spent a stand alone post to point out that someone shouldn't disagree unless they were willing to argue over it for an additional 20 thread pages. And disagreeing is showing that you have a stake in it, it is important to know where people stand on various issues, even if they don't feel like composing a 6 paragraph response detailing with exact quotes why someone is wrong. I made my point, sure, yet it was apparently misunderstood since the argument was carried on afterwards regardless, necessitating my need to restate that I wasn't going to bother arguing that specific point even though I explicitly disagreed with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I &quot;spent&quot; a post (because it's an infinite resource, so I'm not sure how I would be capable of 'spending' it) to point out that your position had been stated and you were stating it again, in a seeming pathological need at having the last word, without adding anything to the discussion.<br /> <br /> Forgive me for not taking the time to go thru the hoops and leaps to multiquote in this Forum's excuse for an UI.<br /> <br /> I wager you're gonna state it once again, in your follow up.<br /> <br /> Please, do ask the moderators to lock the thread if it's existence bothers you so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T06:45:59-08:00","id":806969,"title":"","content":"So what have we learned? Weres are still broken for reasons I'll never understand. It is why I dislike the splat.<br /> I mean they get <b>double their power stat</b> to resist mind control? WTF! Whose brain dead idea was that?<br /> Talk about Twinking! That would go in any crossover. No one's power stat should be better anyones elses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T06:49:28-08:00","id":806973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806969#post806969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what have we learned? Weres are still broken for reasons I'll never understand. It is why I dislike the splat.<br /> I mean they get <b>double their power stat</b> to resist mind control? WTF! Whose brain dead idea was that?<br /> Talk about Twinking! That would go in any crossover. No one's power stat should be better anyones elses.</div> </div> </div> </div>My troll senses are tingling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:06:30-08:00","id":806982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806969#post806969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what have we learned? Weres are still broken for reasons I'll never understand. It is why I dislike the splat. I mean they get <b>double their power stat</b> to resist mind control? WTF! Whose brain dead idea was that? Talk about Twinking! That would go in any crossover. No one's power stat should be better anyones elses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing is broken.<br /> <br /> The rule about doubling the power stat only applies during Death Rage. In any other scenario, Dominate, Nightmare and Majesty are all incredibly, incredibly powerful. If it makes you feel any better, Vampires are practically immune to mindcontrol during Frenzy. And they add their Potency to their attack rolls. The powerstats are all just different, better in some areas and not others.<br /> <br /> Besides, Mages are still Mages. Save your energy for a few months when Mage 2e comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:08:35-08:00","id":806984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806967#post806967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I &quot;spent&quot; a post (because it's an infinite resource, so I'm not sure how I would be capable of 'spending' it) to point out that your position had been stated and you were stating it again, in a seeming pathological need at having the last word, without adding anything to the discussion.<br /> <br /> Forgive me for not taking the time to go thru the hoops and leaps to multiquote in this Forum's excuse for an UI.<br /> <br /> I wager you're gonna state it once again, in your follow up.<br /> <br /> Please, do ask the moderators to lock the thread if it's existence bothers you so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I restated my position because the person I was discussing things with at the time continued trying to argue with me about a subject that I had already stated I wasn't interested in debating at the time. Which, caused me to restate firmly and without excess that I did not agree with their position, yet was unwilling to type up an essay explaining why. <br /> <br /> I have no problem with the thread in general, what I am beginning to have a problem with, however, is you. You were the one butting into a discussion that was already all but over with, not to state your stance on what was being discussed or to add any kind of insight into the topic at hand, but to tell the side you didn't agree with to stop posting. Why? Because you didn't like it? I'd wager that I was adding more to the discussion even just by restating my position than posts like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806973#post806973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My troll senses are tingling.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:46:13-08:00","id":807014,"title":"","content":"In Ephsy's defense on the troll sense thing... that probably was trolling from Chattnos, in a humor type way. But otherwise I agree with you Ashen (that seems pretty awkward to say as it usually seems we're on opposite sides of things about werewolves).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:08:57-08:00","id":807062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=806982#post806982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, Mages are still Mages. Save your energy for a few months when Mage 2e comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That should be an interesting can of worms. If people are that upset over double the Supernatural Resistance to change your mind while in Kuruth, I imagine they won't be pleased about most spells ignoring Supernatural Resistance altogether.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm looking forward to getting into the second edition, it seems like an improvement over the first, but I doubt it'll reach the level of interest I have in Vampire and Werewolf and Hunter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:23:36-08:00","id":807075,"title":"","content":"So my issue with these types of threads is that they become a case of constantly wandering goal posts where people pull out the exact power to counter a thing some other poster said. I feel like our efforts are better suited first establishing some definitions. Someone who is better with Werewolf should make a full pack with 5 Uratha, 5 supporting Wolf-Blooded and 10 supporting Humans per the rules for pack creation that is geared towards the idea of taking and holding territory at... lets say 15 XP, because the vamp book puts starting Ancillae at that.<br /> <br /> There will be some back and forth as we decide on how exactly to make these wolves. Once that is hammered out, possibly with a variant or two, we can start talking about Vampire's answers to that question.<br /> <br /> As to the whole detect vampires / detect werewolves thing? Magic Does What It Says on the Tin. Extrapolation and &quot;logical conclusions&quot; are generally bad form in these types of threads. If Werewolves do not have an ability that specifically calls out being able to detect Vampires, then they do not. Why? Because magic. Something something skin soaked in lies or whatever. No amount of explaining why they logically &quot;should&quot; have this abilities matters. I am perfectly certain that even if I do not have the counter for why they shouldn't, such a counter from someone sufficiently eloquent and persuasive exists. Empirically speaking, however, they don't have it. Turn your creative energy towards explaining why that is instead of explaining why they should get free stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:28:20-08:00","id":807079,"title":"","content":"They do have that special ability though. It's called &quot;Wolf Senses.&quot; By your logic, they can't detect cars because they lack a car detection power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:04:04-08:00","id":807192,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but please point out in the book where it says wolf senses automatically detects vampires in a crowd without knowing what to look for and without getting up close and personal in regard to scent(And that specifies each other and wolfblooded). Also, where are people getting the know what they ate and shit from wolf senses?<br /> <br /> The detecting cars analogy is asinine at best, it is more apt to say a specific make and model in the middle of a junkyard in most cases that you would be encountering most vampires. Vampires look human, act human, and mingle in groups of humans, and often surround themselves with humans. You MIGHT be able to apply wolf senses, but it would require knowing what to look for (and hoping things like blush of life isn't on), and general scrutiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T15:07:46-08:00","id":807335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=807192#post807192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but please point out in the book where it says wolf senses automatically detects vampires in a crowd without knowing what to look for and without getting up close and personal in regard to scent(And that specifies each other and wolfblooded).</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly wouldn't say automatic. Given the opportunity, a werewolf <i>could </i>notice, but it's not going to be so easy most of the time. Werewolves are hunters. They really don't let things come to them. Everything they want, they earn. You go out and hunt prey. You use your senses, you study the prey with human reason, you investigate as only a werewolf can. Theirs is an endlessly active life, so I think if they're going to find out, they need to really get in there in the dirt and grime and blood to do it.<br /> <br /> Vampires might inadvertently make it easier sometimes, but I think most of the time they wouldn't. The blush of life is really potent for disguising oneself, even from werewolves, who'd then have to get <i>really </i>up close and personal or something else would have to tip them off for them to have a chance (unless they use Scent the Unnatural).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=807192#post807192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, where are people getting the know what they ate and shit from wolf senses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolves and dogs can do this with great facility. That's where folks are getting it from; we didn't have room in the 2E core to fit in everything we might have wanted, like a detailed breakdown of exactly what lupine senses do, but painted a pretty good picture of how they transform a werewolf's perception. A dog can go in your room and know when you last slept in your bed and who was with you. They can smell you and know what you last ate. They can get a lot of similarly interesting information from your, ahem, spoor. Wolves are like that except they're predators by nature, driven to hunt to survive. So they're quite used to getting vital information about potential prey or rivals that way.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T16:19:34-08:00","id":807401,"title":"","content":"I think we're pretty much in agreement then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T17:44:49-08:00","id":807459,"title":"","content":"Anyways. Focus here is that we need an actual, realistic pack of five 15xp uratha (one of each auspice) supported by five wolf blooded and ten humans per the pack creation rules on page 91. The pack should be focused on conquering and holding territory.<br /> <br /> Not certain I have the expertise to do optimized werewolf.<br /> <br /> I would like to establish &quot;no combat related professional training for either side&quot; since that merit tends to overwhelm other aspects of the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 01-12-2016, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:41:05-08:00","id":807922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=807335#post807335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I certainly wouldn't say automatic. Given the opportunity, a werewolf <i>could </i>notice, but it's not going to be so easy most of the time. Werewolves are hunters. They really don't let things come to them. Everything they want, they earn. You go out and hunt prey. You use your senses, you study the prey with human reason, you investigate as only a werewolf can. Theirs is an endlessly active life, so I think if they're going to find out, they need to really get in there in the dirt and grime and blood to do it.<br /> <br /> Vampires might inadvertently make it easier sometimes, but I think most of the time they wouldn't. The blush of life is really potent for disguising oneself, even from werewolves, who'd then have to get <i>really </i>up close and personal or something else would have to tip them off for them to have a chance (unless they use Scent the Unnatural).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wolves and dogs can do this with great facility. That's where folks are getting it from; we didn't have room in the 2E core to fit in everything we might have wanted, like a detailed breakdown of exactly what lupine senses do, but painted a pretty good picture of how they transform a werewolf's perception. A dog can go in your room and know when you last slept in your bed and who was with you. They can smell you and know what you last ate. They can get a lot of similarly interesting information from your, ahem, spoor. Wolves are like that except they're predators by nature, driven to hunt to survive. So they're quite used to getting vital information about potential prey or rivals that way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yet dogs still sniff each others butts(I own six). So yeah if a were wants to try to sniff my vamps ass to tell if is human or not, go ahead!<br /> The still sniff scat. They pick traces i the air or on ground but even they still close to identify.<br /> <br /> PS Dogs eyesight poorer than a humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 01-13-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:32:13-08:00","id":807955,"title":"","content":"Here, I'll try and start us off. Here is a Rahu and an Irraka. Assuming each Uratha purchases Totem 3, Safe Place 1 and Dedicated Locus 1 for the whole pack and each Wolf-Blooded will purchase Totem 1.<br /> <br /> TOTEM BONUS: Residential Area 5, Staff [Firearms, Weaponry, Brawl] 3, Brawl +1<br /> <br /> RAHU BLOOD TALON<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div s