>Equipment</b></span></span><br /> Bullet Proof Vest (1/3 Armor)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>EXP</b></span></span><br /> 5 Gift of Evasion<br /> 3 Purity 3<br /> 5 Primal Urge 2<br /> 2 Efficient Killer<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> IRRAKA IRON MASTER<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Basic Information </span></span></b><br /> Auspice: Irraka<br /> Tribe: Iron Master<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Anchors</b></span></span><br /> Human Touchstone:<br /> Spirit Touchstone:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attributes</b></span></span><br /> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 2<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> Presence 1, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Skills </b></span></span><br /> Politics 4<br /> Athletics 2, Brawl [Grapple] 4, Larceny [Breaking and Entering] 3, Stealth [Ambush] 3<br /> Subterfuge 4, Streetwise 3<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Advantages </b></span></span><br /> Renown: Cunning 2, Purity 1<br /> Gifts: No Moon 3, Evasion (Hit and Run), Stealth (Shadow Pelt, Pack Stalks the Prey), Warding (All Doors Locked, Maze Ward)<br /> Rituals:<br /> Merits: Totem 3, Safe Place 1, Dedicated Locus 1, Sounds of the City 2, Fading 3, Flanking 2, Residential Area 5, Staff [Weaponry, Firearms, Brawl] 3<br /> Primal Urge: 1 (10/1, 1B)<br /> Harmony: 5<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Derived Traits</b></span></span><br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Health: 8<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Initiative: 5<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Equipment</b></span></span><br /> Bullet Proof Vest (1/3 Armor)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>EXP</b></span></span><br /> 3 Honor 1<br /> 5 Warding<br /> 3 Cunning 3<br /> 2 Flanking<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 01-13-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:42:30-08:00","id":807963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=807459#post807459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways. Focus here is that we need an actual, realistic pack of five 15xp uratha (one of each auspice) supported by five wolf blooded and ten humans per the pack creation rules on page 91. The pack should be focused on conquering and holding territory.<br /> <br /> Not certain I have the expertise to do optimized werewolf.<br /> <br /> I would like to establish &quot;no combat related professional training for either side&quot; since that merit tends to overwhelm other aspects of the character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This doesn't sound like a realistic pack to me. Sounds more like an ideal pack. In reality packs have gaps. Also packs that focus on conquering territory are going to run into problems very quickly. Remember that for Werewolves only local power is very strong while its pretty middling for Vampires (Coteries). On the other hand Vampires have supreme hegemonic power at the highest levels. Packs are very weak against federal interference, unless you plan to run some kind of Werewolf apocalypse against all humanity type of game. <br /> <br /> The thing about violence is that it always has consequences. Consequences is the key to running successful cross-over chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:51:34-08:00","id":807970,"title":"","content":"While ideal, it is, I feel, realistic enough to see actual play as NPCs if not PCs. It is okay if it is a bit unrealistically coordinated for purposes of discussion. The idea is to keep it realistic enough while also being optimized enough to be useful for our purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T12:49:09-08:00","id":808147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=807922#post807922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet dogs still sniff each others butts(I own six). So yeah if a were wants to try to sniff my vamps ass to tell if is human or not, go ahead!<br /> The still sniff scat. They pick traces i the air or on ground but even they still close to identify.<br /> <br /> PS Dogs eyesight poorer than a humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of that is range, part of it is ritual. But yes, if a dog notices an interesting smell, they do get closer to investigate. I didn't say otherwise. But werewolf senses are potent enough that they can certainly tell a lot even at a distance.<br /> <br /> Dogs have better nightvision than humans do and see motion more clearly. Werewolves aren't like dogs or wolves, since they have the best of both worlds. A dog's eyesight might be worse than a human's for the most part, but a werewolf's is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T21:49:32-08:00","id":810961,"title":"","content":"I have an odd question to all of this. Would Dominate function against a spirit?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T22:29:53-08:00","id":810974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=810961#post810961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an odd question to all of this. Would Dominate function against a spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. See page 125 of the alpha release of Chronicles of Darkness. Resistance is used instead of specific resistance traits like resolve. Rank is used as the Supernatural Tolerance attribute, in place of Blood Potency. <br /> <br /> (It's not specified anywhere I can see, but I'd assume you can't Dominate a spirit and command them to break their ban.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T05:17:51-08:00","id":811068,"title":"","content":"You can no more command a spirit to break its ban than you could command a human to fly.<br /> <br /> Oh, and you can't dominate an idigam. They're immune to that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T05:46:54-08:00","id":811075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/799156-2e-werewolf-crossover-questions?p=811068#post811068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can no more command a spirit to break its ban than you could command a human to fly.<br /> <br /> Oh, and you can't dominate an idigam. They're immune to that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it actually stated somewhere that you can't mind control spirits into breaking their bans or is this just something people assume (Which is seeming to happen on these forums more and more)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}